WEBVTT

00:31.365 --> 00:33.834
Ah!

00:33.967 --> 00:37.271
- Almost there, Bronco.
- Fuck! Agh!

00:37.405 --> 00:39.039
Gucci, we are inbound.

00:39.173 --> 00:40.574
Understood.

00:41.175 --> 00:43.544
Rachel, stay in the car.
Stay down.

00:43.677 --> 00:44.645
- Okay. Yeah.
- Moreno!

00:45.045 --> 00:46.046
- On it!
- Let's go! Let's go...

00:46.214 --> 00:47.915
- Baker, on me!
- Got it!

00:48.216 --> 00:50.351
- Gucci, how long?
- I need another minute!

00:50.484 --> 00:53.521
- We don't have a minute!
- Guch, hurry your ass up!

00:53.654 --> 00:56.357
- UAV incoming!
- Dunne? Get out of there!

00:56.524 --> 00:57.991
Everyone down!

01:05.233 --> 01:07.435
My name is Rachel Wild.

01:08.536 --> 01:10.104
I'm a particular type
of lawyer.

01:12.606 --> 01:15.776
My job is to dog and chase down
those that hide their debts

01:15.909 --> 01:18.546
through legal loopholes
and shell companies.

01:21.682 --> 01:24.452
I work between the moral
and the immoral.

01:27.087 --> 01:30.324
The legal and the illegal.

01:30.558 --> 01:32.560
The black and the white.

01:34.128 --> 01:36.530
I operate in the grey.

01:48.442 --> 01:50.311
- Hello?
- Hey, Bobby. I've got some news.

01:50.444 --> 01:52.846
- Braxton?
- Hey, are you there, Bobby?

01:52.980 --> 01:55.783
No, I'm losing you.

01:55.916 --> 01:58.919
The man on the phone
taught me everything I know.

01:59.052 --> 02:00.754
Hey, driver,
can you find me a signal?

02:00.888 --> 02:01.822
Of course.

02:09.830 --> 02:11.965
Do you wanna go, er,
stretch your legs?

02:13.100 --> 02:13.934
Okay.

02:19.440 --> 02:20.641
Shall I give you a minute, boss?

02:21.141 --> 02:22.276
Thank you, John.

02:29.283 --> 02:30.784
Bobby, are you there?

02:31.084 --> 02:33.454
- Braxton, what you got?
- I got a meeting.

02:33.587 --> 02:35.623
- With who?
- Salazar.

02:36.324 --> 02:37.291
You got a meeting
with Salazar?

02:37.425 --> 02:38.692
That's not all I got.

02:39.126 --> 02:40.561
Where's this going, Braxton?

02:40.994 --> 02:43.397
Where would
you like this to go, hm?

02:43.531 --> 02:44.365
Don't tease me.

02:45.699 --> 02:48.369
- How much?
- Full debt plus interest.

02:51.004 --> 02:53.040
That's impossible.
I don't believe you.

02:53.173 --> 02:55.008
Well, I got the leverage.
I got the agreement.

02:55.142 --> 02:56.910
I got the paperwork
and I got the signature.

02:57.044 --> 02:59.112
- After this, I owe you nothing.
- Uh-huh.

02:59.480 --> 03:01.181
- We're done.
- Yeah.

03:01.549 --> 03:03.351
Olsson will take you back
to your hotel.

03:05.219 --> 03:08.689
How do you do it?
Braxton, if you pull this off--

03:09.290 --> 03:10.724
you get the full 5%.

03:11.825 --> 03:13.026
Where are you?

03:13.160 --> 03:15.028
I'm on Salazar's island.

03:15.162 --> 03:17.565
- I'll be in New York tonight.
- No trouble?

03:17.698 --> 03:20.300
Nah, I got John
with me for security.

03:20.301 --> 03:21.569
You're on his island

03:22.069 --> 03:23.237
and you only have
one man for security?

03:23.371 --> 03:25.038
You just let me
worry about that.

03:25.172 --> 03:27.908
Show your p-- Oh, Jesus.

03:28.141 --> 03:30.210
- Braxton?
- Fuck! Fuck...

03:32.913 --> 03:34.315
What's happening?

03:35.316 --> 03:36.484
Can you hear me?

03:37.385 --> 03:39.019
Braxton, what's happening?

03:43.724 --> 03:44.658
Braxton, are you there?

03:46.093 --> 03:47.695
Can you hear me?

04:00.674 --> 04:02.410
The upside of
this job is that when you win,

04:03.544 --> 04:04.545
you win big.

04:06.179 --> 04:07.881
The downside is that
when you lose,

04:09.450 --> 04:10.884
you end up in a hole
in the ground.

04:20.060 --> 04:22.930
Mr. Salazar,
the contract is void.

04:23.063 --> 04:25.999
Good! If Spencer Goldstein
think they're getting

04:26.133 --> 04:29.403
their billion dollars back,
they can go fuck themselves.

04:30.304 --> 04:33.741
And if they send anyone else
to try, we'll take care of them.

04:37.445 --> 04:40.013
My clients
are asset managers,

04:40.414 --> 04:42.683
basically sophisticated
bankers.

04:43.150 --> 04:45.285
They make money
by loaning money

04:45.419 --> 04:46.887
and when they make mistakes,

04:47.154 --> 04:49.523
they subcontract to people
like Braxton.

04:49.657 --> 04:51.024
Or people like me.

04:51.559 --> 04:53.527
If the first mouse gets sloppy,

04:53.894 --> 04:55.963
then it's the second mouse
that gets the cheese.

04:56.163 --> 04:57.931
Wait, Miss Wild!

04:58.298 --> 04:59.533
It's under control,
Mr. Goldstein.

04:59.667 --> 05:01.369
Wait, Miss Wild!
Please!

05:01.502 --> 05:03.504
- You should have called, Bobby.
- Sorry, Miss Sheen.

05:03.637 --> 05:04.905
We scheduled?

05:05.138 --> 05:06.374
Well, given what happened
to Braxton,

05:06.507 --> 05:07.875
I think we are now.

05:08.308 --> 05:10.544
- I don't have time now.
- Oh, yes. Yes, you do.

05:10.678 --> 05:11.812
I'm here to make you money.

05:13.847 --> 05:14.848
I'll call you back.

05:16.617 --> 05:18.218
Thanks, ladies. Two minutes.

05:18.652 --> 05:20.588
And don't throw any shit
in this direction.

05:21.855 --> 05:25.559
Why didn't you let him know what
he was getting himself into?

05:25.793 --> 05:27.327
Nobody knew what
he was getting into.

05:27.461 --> 05:28.596
- Hm.
- Anyway, what's it got

05:28.762 --> 05:31.098
- to do with you?
- I liked Braxton.

05:31.765 --> 05:34.201
But I didn't like the
hand grenade you passed him.

05:36.169 --> 05:39.206
Manny Salazar. He's not really
the guy you loan

05:39.339 --> 05:41.575
a billion dollars and expect
to see it back.

05:42.209 --> 05:43.811
- You weren't thorough, Bobby.
- What did I just say

05:43.944 --> 05:45.913
- about throwing shit?
- I'm just here to give you

05:46.046 --> 05:47.881
an opportunity
to recover your money.

05:48.115 --> 05:50.584
- You think you can recover it?
- You know I can.

05:50.818 --> 05:52.653
Ooh, but I know
you're too expensive.

05:52.786 --> 05:55.723
Wouldn't Spencer Goldstein
rather see its money back

05:55.856 --> 05:58.191
and stop putting bodies
in the ground?

05:58.325 --> 05:59.226
Careful.

05:59.393 --> 06:00.360
You're pretty-ish,

06:00.494 --> 06:01.895
and funny-ish, and clever.

06:02.029 --> 06:03.764
But you're not
that fucking clever.

06:03.997 --> 06:07.000
Hire someone else, you're...
well, repeating the same mistake

06:07.167 --> 06:09.837
you made with Braxton
and getting the same result.

06:11.672 --> 06:13.874
- On what terms?
- Standard sub-contract.

06:14.007 --> 06:16.577
You get deniability, Spencer
Goldstein's hands stay clean.

06:16.710 --> 06:19.813
And you only pay me
if I recover the full debt.

06:20.213 --> 06:22.082
- How much?
- Twenty percent.

06:22.215 --> 06:24.918
- I can get this done for five.
- By who?

06:26.186 --> 06:29.256
You get people killed for five
and you're still left short.

06:29.389 --> 06:31.158
You know,
I really don't like you.

06:31.592 --> 06:33.527
You'll save a dollar
to lose a hundred.

06:33.661 --> 06:34.828
You're a fucking nuisance.

06:36.430 --> 06:37.765
Of course
I'm a fucking nuisance.

06:38.832 --> 06:42.269
I can do it for 7.5%.

06:42.436 --> 06:44.705
Ten percent.
And ten million upfront.

06:45.673 --> 06:47.975
I don't trust you, and...

06:48.108 --> 06:50.343
well, you need skin in the game.

06:53.280 --> 06:54.281
I can make that work.

06:57.350 --> 06:59.453
That was easy.

06:59.587 --> 07:01.254
Don't you have
to call your boss first?

07:04.191 --> 07:05.926
I don't have to call upstairs.

07:06.093 --> 07:06.794
Impressive!

07:08.596 --> 07:11.131
Every time I visit,
you're a floor higher.

07:11.264 --> 07:13.601
You however do need
a bigger office.

07:14.367 --> 07:15.435
Love you, Bobby.

07:17.404 --> 07:18.572
Fuck you, Rachel.

07:23.276 --> 07:27.114
Asset managers. I'm telling you,
they own the lot.

07:27.380 --> 07:30.217
I have an asset manager
who manages my money.

07:32.486 --> 07:34.955
That's because
in spite of what you look like,

07:35.355 --> 07:36.490
you can still think.

07:37.725 --> 07:38.759
But only small picture.

07:40.561 --> 07:43.263
That's why I have a manager
manage my money.

07:51.104 --> 07:52.606
What do you think
they do with it?

07:53.106 --> 07:54.341
I know what they do with it.

07:55.509 --> 07:56.577
They make me more money.

07:56.944 --> 07:57.811
They make you
more money because

07:57.945 --> 07:59.246
they fucking own everything.

07:59.379 --> 08:00.914
I'm happy with that.

08:01.281 --> 08:02.850
You wouldn't be if you knew
what they were up to.

08:03.016 --> 08:04.718
They're out of control.
They run everything.

08:04.852 --> 08:06.486
The news, the views.

08:07.588 --> 08:08.556
The weapons, the wars.

08:08.689 --> 08:09.990
There's no conspiracy.

08:10.123 --> 08:11.992
This is good for me
and bad for you.

08:12.926 --> 08:14.227
You should jump in.

08:14.361 --> 08:15.696
The water's warm.

08:16.429 --> 08:18.632
I've worked with Sid
and Bronco for so long,

08:18.799 --> 08:20.834
they're the only two I trust
to keep me alive.

08:22.369 --> 08:24.705
Salazar is a chameleon
who hides behind

08:24.838 --> 08:26.907
hundreds of different
pseudonyms.

08:27.140 --> 08:29.242
Last month,
he was called McIntyre.

08:29.376 --> 08:31.478
The month before that,
Rodriguez.

08:31.612 --> 08:34.047
To corner Salazar,
you must attack him legally

08:34.214 --> 08:35.182
and illegally.

08:35.883 --> 08:37.885
Half my team
deals with the former,

08:38.018 --> 08:38.952
the other half, the latter.

08:39.119 --> 08:40.020
Evening all.

08:40.153 --> 08:40.954
Glover.

08:42.355 --> 08:43.290
Gentlemen.

08:44.324 --> 08:45.793
- Ma'am.
- Ma'am.

08:46.359 --> 08:48.161
Bronco heads
a team that specializes

08:48.295 --> 08:51.264
in extraction,
intimidation and sabotage.

08:51.398 --> 08:54.067
And Sidney's band specializes
in corruption,

08:54.201 --> 08:55.969
bribery and
covert surveillance.

08:56.136 --> 08:57.337
So, er...

08:59.506 --> 09:00.974
Salazar?

09:01.675 --> 09:04.812
Manny Salazar is rare
and unique.

09:04.978 --> 09:07.380
Braxton uncovered some
of his hidden assets.

09:07.514 --> 09:09.282
Salazar then buried
those assets.

09:09.416 --> 09:10.350
Along with Braxton.

09:10.584 --> 09:12.385
So, how do we squeeze him?

09:12.853 --> 09:14.722
- We bring him to the table.
- How do we do that?

09:15.589 --> 09:17.224
Pincer movement.

09:17.357 --> 09:19.326
Combination of practical
and procedural.

09:19.727 --> 09:22.696
Sidney, you will be
going to Saudi.

09:22.830 --> 09:24.231
You, Bronco,

09:24.598 --> 09:25.966
you're coming with me.

09:26.867 --> 09:30.270
First, I must
meet Salazar's infamous lawyer.

09:30.503 --> 09:33.741
I can only do this concealed
in a Trojan horse.

09:34.775 --> 09:37.711
So sorry to have kept
you waiting, Miss Wild.

09:37.878 --> 09:41.181
I do hope my staff
has taken care of you.

09:41.782 --> 09:43.684
I'm fine, Mr. Horowitz.

09:44.251 --> 09:48.922
So, we have had a chance
to look over your proposal.

09:49.389 --> 09:53.460
And I see that you have quite
substantial capital

09:53.627 --> 09:55.228
that you may need help with.

09:59.967 --> 10:00.968
I'm sorry...

10:01.735 --> 10:02.903
and you are?

10:03.737 --> 10:04.872
I don't matter.

10:08.976 --> 10:10.711
Yes, indeed.

10:10.978 --> 10:14.214
I'm particularly interested
in Mr. Salazar's portfolio.

10:17.484 --> 10:19.352
That is private information.

10:19.486 --> 10:21.254
I'm sorry, Sir. Do you mind?

10:21.388 --> 10:22.756
That's very valuable.

10:25.726 --> 10:29.162
Why do I have the feeling there
is another agenda going on here?

10:29.296 --> 10:30.764
- Hm?
- You'd like to hear it?

10:30.898 --> 10:32.499
No. That's another meeting.

10:33.333 --> 10:34.768
We're done here!

10:35.568 --> 10:38.171
Can you call Gary
into my office, please?

10:38.305 --> 10:40.140
There is a situation here.

10:40.273 --> 10:41.709
I assure you,
you'd like to listen.

10:41.842 --> 10:43.076
The alternative is...

10:44.111 --> 10:45.612
very expensive.

10:45.746 --> 10:47.180
Well, I'm not buying
what you're selling.

10:47.347 --> 10:49.082
Gary! Gary!

10:56.623 --> 10:58.358
Mr. Horowitz,
is there a problem?

10:58.491 --> 11:00.127
Yeah. Get them out
of my office, now.

11:00.660 --> 11:03.163
Ma'am, Sir,
if you'd like to follow...

11:03.296 --> 11:05.198
Gary, a moment.

11:05.966 --> 11:08.068
There are two versions of how
this narrative plays out.

11:08.601 --> 11:10.570
Version one, Gary waits
patiently and quietly

11:10.704 --> 11:12.339
by the door for the next
30 seconds

11:12.472 --> 11:14.141
while we conclude our business.

11:14.274 --> 11:17.177
And then we leave in a calm
and orderly fashion.

11:18.045 --> 11:21.514
Version two, Gary steps forward
on a reckless endeavour

11:21.648 --> 11:25.451
and you spend the next six hours
sponging him off the walls.

11:25.452 --> 11:27.154
I know which version
Gary would prefer.

11:31.491 --> 11:34.427
You... I... you have...
I... I...

11:34.561 --> 11:35.362
Gary.

11:36.396 --> 11:37.330
Shh.

11:40.200 --> 11:41.301
Gary?

11:42.169 --> 11:44.872
Maybe it's better if you just
take a few steps back.

11:49.409 --> 11:52.846
I'm here for the debt that
Salazar owes Spencer Goldstein.

11:53.013 --> 11:55.582
As his lawyer, I'm pretty sure
you know where all

11:55.715 --> 11:58.385
his proxy corporations
and shell companies are.

11:58.986 --> 12:01.121
This is an opportunity
for you to work with me

12:01.254 --> 12:03.590
so we can find a more
amicable agreement.

12:05.759 --> 12:07.460
I think it's time
for you to leave.

12:07.761 --> 12:09.262
Well, if I can't have
this conversation with you,

12:09.396 --> 12:11.698
I guess I'll have it
with Salazar himself.

12:12.432 --> 12:15.235
Don't get into water
that you can't swim in.

12:16.603 --> 12:17.938
Likewise.

12:18.405 --> 12:20.673
And if you get
into any trouble, please...

12:21.608 --> 12:22.575
call me.

12:23.443 --> 12:24.744
I'm known to be...

12:25.612 --> 12:26.379
very effective.

12:28.849 --> 12:30.517
Rachel Wild. That's my number.

12:30.784 --> 12:32.152
You can call me anytime.

12:32.285 --> 12:34.054
Have a wonderful day,
Mr. Horowitz.

12:34.354 --> 12:35.522
Thanks, Gary.

12:41.361 --> 12:42.295
Are we clear on the plan?

12:44.364 --> 12:45.432
Phase one.

12:45.565 --> 12:47.534
Procedural and practical.

12:47.868 --> 12:50.237
Bronco and Baker will
travel to Salazar's island

12:50.370 --> 12:53.373
on a commercial flight
while it's still safe to do so.

12:53.573 --> 12:55.608
They need to start sabotaging
Salazar's interests

12:55.742 --> 12:57.477
and set up a base
a month before

12:57.610 --> 12:59.479
I will eventually arrive
for a meeting.

12:59.880 --> 13:01.348
While Sid flies to Saudi

13:01.481 --> 13:03.516
to start
his corruption process.

13:04.151 --> 13:07.420
His anonymous phone call will
tip off the Saudi authorities.

13:08.621 --> 13:10.457
Salazar's hotel in Jeddah
got approval

13:10.623 --> 13:14.593
to build 130,000 square feet.

13:14.594 --> 13:16.029
But the real blueprint shows

13:16.163 --> 13:19.032
he's building
150,000 square feet.

13:19.166 --> 13:20.533
Hello...

13:21.234 --> 13:22.769
The tip-off will let
the ministry know

13:22.903 --> 13:24.771
that he's in breach
of planning consent.

13:24.905 --> 13:26.840
That'll do the job.

13:26.974 --> 13:29.376
The Saudis will take
this seriously and shut down

13:29.509 --> 13:31.511
construction while the
paperwork gets reorganized.

13:31.644 --> 13:33.246
They are measuring
the building.

13:33.646 --> 13:35.815
- We are being closed down.
- Hold on, please.

13:35.949 --> 13:38.251
Horowitz will be
fielding phone calls

13:38.518 --> 13:40.387
and he'll get his wings clipped.

13:40.520 --> 13:43.490
Why have I got the foreman
of our Saudi construction site

13:43.623 --> 13:47.694
saying that we have been shut
down for a size discrepancy?

13:47.861 --> 13:49.829
He will be penalized
somewhere in the region of...

13:49.963 --> 13:51.965
...$4 million a week.

13:52.132 --> 13:54.567
Someone is fucking with us.

13:54.767 --> 13:55.835
It's that woman.

13:56.003 --> 13:57.404
I bet it's that fucking woman.

13:57.804 --> 14:00.340
While he's busy
putting out that fire,

14:01.141 --> 14:04.711
Sidney will be on stage two
of his corruption campaign.

14:04.878 --> 14:07.047
There is a forensic skill
to bribery

14:07.180 --> 14:08.982
and Sid is the best surgeon
I've ever had

14:09.149 --> 14:10.117
the pleasure to witness.

14:10.283 --> 14:11.952
If you're gonna corrupt someone,

14:12.219 --> 14:14.421
there's a right way and a wrong
way of going about it.

14:15.388 --> 14:17.991
And what's wrong exactly
about putting 25 grand

14:18.158 --> 14:19.492
in someone's pocket?

14:19.893 --> 14:21.561
I think as long as you
do it elegantly.

14:21.794 --> 14:24.364
You can't just shove 25 grand
in someone's hand.

14:24.497 --> 14:25.398
Doesn't work.

14:26.733 --> 14:27.867
What you need is lube.

14:28.001 --> 14:28.969
An alibi.

14:29.202 --> 14:31.204
Something to make them feel...

14:31.338 --> 14:32.472
positive about the transaction.

14:35.375 --> 14:36.309
Oopsy daisy.

14:46.719 --> 14:47.854
I am so sorry.

14:47.988 --> 14:49.156
That is totally my fault.

14:51.724 --> 14:53.626
Don't worry,
there's hardly any damages.

14:53.760 --> 14:55.228
Oh, you don't know that.

14:55.495 --> 14:57.530
There are sensors,
there's the chassis rail...

14:57.664 --> 14:58.531
and are you okay?

14:59.532 --> 15:00.700
I'm fine.

15:01.834 --> 15:04.171
It can take up to two days
for whiplash to bite.

15:05.838 --> 15:06.906
My friend's a doctor.

15:08.175 --> 15:09.409
He'll take a look at you.

15:10.210 --> 15:11.478
Stand on one foot, please.

15:11.611 --> 15:12.679
And close your eyes.

15:15.715 --> 15:17.584
Ooh, I don't like
the look of that.

15:18.118 --> 15:20.287
Oh dear. You'll have to see
a physiotherapist.

15:20.420 --> 15:21.921
Don't worry,
we'll take care of it.

15:22.055 --> 15:24.157
There is a note
inside the envelope

15:24.291 --> 15:26.059
from the doctor
that'll tell you exactly

15:26.226 --> 15:28.161
how to make a full recovery.

15:28.395 --> 15:29.129
And remember...

15:30.197 --> 15:31.564
that can take six weeks.

15:33.466 --> 15:35.668
That port superintendent
is under the spell

15:35.802 --> 15:38.038
of old fashioned cash,

15:38.305 --> 15:39.439
has a perfect alibi...

15:41.141 --> 15:42.375
and clear instructions

15:42.542 --> 15:45.245
on how to make a year's salary

15:45.378 --> 15:46.346
in six weeks.

15:46.479 --> 15:47.780
All I need is a thumbs up.

15:48.215 --> 15:50.483
One, and he's on the hook.

15:50.717 --> 15:52.919
Two, and he'll suck your cock.

16:01.061 --> 16:02.629
You're in luck, Gucci.

16:02.996 --> 16:04.531
Now, the port
superintendent can justify

16:04.664 --> 16:06.199
why he has a year's salary
tax free.

16:06.333 --> 16:08.468
Your steel is impounded.

16:08.601 --> 16:10.037
The paperwork doesn't match.

16:10.170 --> 16:12.105
What do you mean, impounded?

16:12.239 --> 16:14.007
Well, get it un-impounded.

16:15.575 --> 16:18.645
That fucking woman
has locked up our steel!

16:18.778 --> 16:21.948
By now, Horowitz should be
getting more bad news

16:22.182 --> 16:26.186
because 20,000 tonnes of steel
are stuck in limbo

16:26.419 --> 16:28.688
and leaves 2,000 construction
workers with nothing to do

16:28.821 --> 16:30.557
but to sunbathe on full pay.

16:31.024 --> 16:32.859
Penalties and delays will cost
them in the region

16:33.026 --> 16:34.761
of $5 million a week.

16:34.927 --> 16:37.464
Now he's burning up in Saudi.

16:37.597 --> 16:39.166
Let's throw him off balance.

16:39.366 --> 16:41.301
Light another fire on his flank.

16:41.534 --> 16:44.504
Next we need to attack his
business on his Spanish island.

16:44.637 --> 16:45.938
What about the oil rig?

16:46.139 --> 16:48.841
It's literally
on Salazar's doorstep.

16:49.476 --> 16:51.644
What do you think Bronco
and Baker are doing?

16:52.545 --> 16:53.613
Javier.

16:54.714 --> 16:55.782
Bronco.

16:56.049 --> 16:57.650
That's my associate, Baker.

16:58.017 --> 16:59.952
Apparently you're the man
that can source anything.

17:00.120 --> 17:01.288
Can you help us?

17:01.554 --> 17:03.290
I can get you what you want.

17:03.823 --> 17:05.125
First thing we need
is hard hats.

17:08.395 --> 17:10.797
Tomorrow's delivery
is the blowout preventer.

17:10.997 --> 17:12.099
We can level that
before it gets there.

17:12.232 --> 17:13.833
No, that's too clumsy.

17:14.967 --> 17:16.603
It's harder to deal with
a mouse in the house

17:16.736 --> 17:18.004
than a gorilla in the villa.

17:19.206 --> 17:20.673
If they can't see the problem,

17:21.174 --> 17:22.309
they can't fix the problem.

17:23.410 --> 17:25.145
Forensic sabotage.

17:25.712 --> 17:29.282
I want them lost in the weeds
for months.

17:30.049 --> 17:34.221
A 200,000 tonne oil rig
will now be rendered redundant

17:34.421 --> 17:36.123
through a Trojan mouse.

17:36.423 --> 17:39.559
A 25 gram Jekyll and Hyde
super fuse.

17:39.692 --> 17:41.394
Yeah, that's our end done, Sir.

17:41.828 --> 17:44.197
All it needs now is to give
the safety inspectors

17:44.331 --> 17:47.033
a little nudge
in the right direction.

17:47.167 --> 17:49.936
Once they find out the rig's
got a fail-safe malfunction...

17:54.841 --> 17:56.776
Doesn't drill, doesn't move

17:56.909 --> 17:57.877
and Salazar's leaking

17:58.044 --> 17:59.412
half a million dollars a day.

18:01.348 --> 18:04.050
He will now be aware he has
quite a significant challenge.

18:05.785 --> 18:08.288
I asked you to take care
of Spencer Goldstein.

18:08.888 --> 18:11.624
And you assured me that
the issue was dead and buried.

18:12.559 --> 18:17.096
Yet somehow I'm now paying
three fucking million dollars

18:17.264 --> 18:19.432
a fucking week for
a fucking oil rig

18:19.566 --> 18:21.268
that doesn't produce
any fucking oil!

18:22.802 --> 18:25.605
So, what I want to know is, A...

18:26.239 --> 18:28.508
who specifically
is doing this to me?

18:28.941 --> 18:31.944
And B, what the fuck
are you doing about it, William?

18:33.112 --> 18:34.681
It is a woman.

18:38.785 --> 18:41.354
With an extremely capable team.

18:42.222 --> 18:45.358
They're cunning, they're clever
and they're efficient.

18:45.625 --> 18:47.126
I'm afraid that they're
gonna continue to be

18:47.260 --> 18:48.761
a very big problem.

19:01.508 --> 19:02.475
Here, William.

19:13.085 --> 19:15.722
Will they continue to be
a problem

19:16.122 --> 19:17.324
if they're no longer alive?

19:18.491 --> 19:19.259
Yes.

19:21.027 --> 19:22.862
She's already insured
against that.

19:23.296 --> 19:28.000
Cut off her head and
there'll be 20 prepaid lawyers

19:28.134 --> 19:29.702
waiting to keep
this thing alive.

19:30.503 --> 19:32.138
And I'm afraid if that happens,

19:32.339 --> 19:35.542
we may be in a mess that will be
impossible to get out of.

19:36.976 --> 19:38.044
What is your advice?

19:40.380 --> 19:41.948
Well, she's, erm...

19:43.783 --> 19:47.153
already costing you about
28 million a month,

19:47.287 --> 19:49.721
so I think it would be
a lot cheaper if...

19:49.722 --> 19:50.790
you can make a deal.

19:51.157 --> 19:52.792
You know, make her an offer.

19:53.860 --> 19:54.661
For how much?

19:56.296 --> 19:58.731
We can ring fence this for...

20:01.067 --> 20:02.168
300 million.

20:07.474 --> 20:09.576
Three hundred million dollars?

20:09.709 --> 20:11.444
- Mm-hm.
- Of my money?

20:11.578 --> 20:12.645
Around that.

20:12.812 --> 20:14.414
You think you're sweating now?

20:14.714 --> 20:16.583
I can make you
fucking sweat, William.

20:16.916 --> 20:18.751
There's only so much
she can find,

20:19.519 --> 20:23.423
and all the really juicy stuff
is still controlled by Wolfgang

20:23.556 --> 20:25.692
and there is no way
she'll ever find that.

20:25.825 --> 20:28.060
Pretty is synonymous
with stupid.

20:28.261 --> 20:30.363
And stupid is synonymous
with naïve.

20:30.530 --> 20:32.699
And naïve is what
I want you to think I am.

20:32.832 --> 20:34.033
During our inaugural meeting,

20:34.166 --> 20:35.935
Bronco placed a bug in his

20:36.068 --> 20:37.604
lawyer of the week award.

20:38.004 --> 20:38.971
Erm, do... do you mind?

20:39.105 --> 20:40.973
That-that's very valuable.

20:41.107 --> 20:42.475
We know who Wolfgang is

20:42.609 --> 20:44.577
because Horowitz
very kindly told us

20:44.711 --> 20:46.145
exactly who he is.

20:46.513 --> 20:48.448
It turns out
he's an accountant.

20:48.581 --> 20:49.749
Wolfgang Klose.

20:49.882 --> 20:52.151
A Harvard-graduated German Arab

20:52.285 --> 20:54.387
who orchestrates
the entire financial empire

20:54.554 --> 20:56.489
from his fortress in Jeddah.

20:56.889 --> 20:58.991
Why is Wolfgang so important
to Salazar?

20:59.125 --> 21:01.561
He's a specialist
that hides his money.

21:01.694 --> 21:03.330
He bounces it around
between countries

21:03.463 --> 21:05.798
and buries it under layers
of shell companies

21:06.032 --> 21:08.234
so it's impossible to find out
who the owner is.

21:08.435 --> 21:10.337
If you can't find
Salazar's money,

21:10.570 --> 21:12.572
you can't recoup the debt.

21:12.705 --> 21:14.807
We need to join those names
to those companies

21:14.941 --> 21:17.777
to untangle Salazar's
administrative opaque soup.

21:18.144 --> 21:19.779
But if we can access
Wolfgang's computer,

21:19.912 --> 21:21.781
we can find where
he's buried the bodies

21:21.914 --> 21:23.950
and Rachel can prove
that he owns the companies.

21:24.083 --> 21:27.086
He recently invited
some ego stroking publications

21:27.219 --> 21:29.856
into his home to tell us
how fantastic, rich

21:29.989 --> 21:32.091
and interesting he is.

21:32.959 --> 21:34.293
The pictures revealed his love

21:34.461 --> 21:36.563
for esoteric '50s sculptures.

21:37.096 --> 21:38.431
While the interview let slip

21:38.598 --> 21:40.933
his profound love
for backgammon.

21:41.300 --> 21:42.201
Did you receive
my gifts?

21:42.335 --> 21:43.436
I'm looking at them now.

21:43.770 --> 21:45.304
Open exhibit A.

21:47.507 --> 21:49.676
- Ooh, loaded dice?
- Precisely.

21:49.809 --> 21:52.345
You got an invite to his party
as a potential investor.

21:52.812 --> 21:54.447
To catch his attention,
you need to win.

21:54.614 --> 21:56.649
- Excuse me, Sir.
- What is it?

21:56.783 --> 21:58.250
There's a guest at
the backgammon table

21:58.385 --> 21:59.819
who hasn't lost a game yet.

21:59.952 --> 22:00.887
Why are you telling me?

22:01.020 --> 22:01.888
Because every time he wins,

22:02.021 --> 22:03.255
he refuses the money.

22:03.523 --> 22:05.191
What's more attractive
to a financier

22:05.324 --> 22:06.726
than a man who refuses money?

22:06.859 --> 22:07.827
How much has he won?

22:07.960 --> 22:09.562
It's over 200,000, Sir.

22:09.696 --> 22:11.097
Having got his attention,

22:11.498 --> 22:13.065
he's going to be looking
at me very dubiously.

22:13.199 --> 22:14.701
So, I'll need to convince him
that I have

22:14.834 --> 22:16.335
no kind of hidden agenda.

22:16.836 --> 22:18.705
Naturally, being the host
and rather paranoid,

22:18.838 --> 22:20.640
he's going to assume that
I'm a grifter and he's the mark.

22:20.773 --> 22:22.341
So, he'll challenge me.

22:22.542 --> 22:24.176
- May I?
- Please.

22:25.845 --> 22:27.814
What do you say,
5,000 a point?

22:28.881 --> 22:29.982
Sure.

22:31.784 --> 22:32.952
Using the loaded dice,

22:33.319 --> 22:34.654
I'll continue
my winning streak.

22:34.854 --> 22:36.823
Simultaneously,
I will refuse payment.

22:37.657 --> 22:39.459
He will insist on paying me.

22:39.892 --> 22:41.728
I make a point
of paying my debts.

22:42.128 --> 22:43.896
But here's where
I make my final move.

22:44.030 --> 22:47.033
You can repay me
by giving me a rematch,

22:47.366 --> 22:48.501
but with a gentleman's bet

22:48.635 --> 22:49.636
and only for $10.

22:50.069 --> 22:51.170
You will lose.

22:51.303 --> 22:52.505
And as a token of a payment,

22:52.639 --> 22:54.373
you will offer him a gift.

22:54.741 --> 22:57.710
It just happens that that gift
is a statue he covets.

22:57.844 --> 22:59.712
Open exhibit B.

23:01.881 --> 23:03.716
In scurries the Trojan rat.

23:05.317 --> 23:07.520
It seems luck has gone my way.

23:07.754 --> 23:08.855
Well played.

23:08.988 --> 23:11.624
Er, rather embarrassingly,

23:11.758 --> 23:13.826
I don't carry that sort of cash.

23:14.193 --> 23:17.096
If you'll allow me, I'll just
pop something in the post?

23:17.564 --> 23:19.799
People are not
suspicious of those that give.

23:19.932 --> 23:21.434
Only those that take.

23:21.568 --> 23:24.804
Sir, a gift has arrived
from Mr. Kershner.

23:24.937 --> 23:27.373
Wolfgang's office
is a Faraday cage,

23:27.507 --> 23:30.276
an impenetrable firewall
preventing anyone or anything

23:30.443 --> 23:31.978
from accessing his data.

23:32.244 --> 23:34.547
However, once you're inside
of said cage

23:34.714 --> 23:36.483
and within 12 feet
of his computer,

23:36.849 --> 23:37.984
we're in his world.

23:38.117 --> 23:39.619
Our statue is a bug,

23:39.752 --> 23:41.988
a camera
and a tempest attack device.

23:42.121 --> 23:43.623
We can start to put names
to companies

23:43.756 --> 23:45.558
and untangle his financial web.

23:45.958 --> 23:48.628
Bob's your uncle,
Fanny's your aunt. We're in.

23:48.895 --> 23:50.296
Now, I'm inside
Wolfgang's world,

23:50.463 --> 23:52.565
we can start to peel back
the onion.

23:53.232 --> 23:54.934
Once I have the legal traction
to freeze some more

23:55.067 --> 23:56.636
of his hidden assets...

23:56.903 --> 23:59.005
Oh, Wolfgang, I've got you now.

23:59.138 --> 24:01.173
...this will accelerate
a desire to reach a deal.

24:01.307 --> 24:02.742
The court approves
the application

24:02.875 --> 24:04.711
to seek international
attachment orders.

24:04.877 --> 24:06.445
Objection, Your Honor!

24:06.613 --> 24:07.780
Overruled!

24:08.214 --> 24:09.315
Thank you, Your Honor.

24:12.284 --> 24:13.686
She's a monster.

24:13.820 --> 24:15.321
However, in order to get

24:15.454 --> 24:17.123
the unpalatable deal
that I want,

24:17.256 --> 24:18.925
I will need to look Salazar
in the eye.

24:19.058 --> 24:19.926
Hello?

24:20.392 --> 24:21.360
Hello?

24:21.494 --> 24:22.461
Oh, Mr. Horowitz,

24:22.629 --> 24:24.462
how lovely to hear from you.

24:24.463 --> 24:25.431
Okay, sweetheart.

24:26.799 --> 24:28.701
200. That's it.

24:28.835 --> 24:31.170
Has anyone ever told you
you have a wonderful timbre

24:31.303 --> 24:32.404
to your voice.

24:33.005 --> 24:34.440
I'm trying to place it.

24:34.574 --> 24:35.441
That's funny?

24:35.642 --> 24:36.676
200 is funny.

24:36.809 --> 24:38.444
I got it.

24:38.645 --> 24:41.213
From the 1950s hit
The African Queen

24:41.347 --> 24:43.850
starring Katherine Hepburn
and Humphrey Bogart.

24:44.016 --> 24:45.985
You sound just like
Katherine Hepburn.

24:46.619 --> 24:47.486
Okay.

24:49.822 --> 24:50.857
300.

24:51.090 --> 24:52.625
I wanna sit down with Salazar.

24:52.759 --> 24:55.094
Since I can't talk to you,
I wanna talk to him.

24:55.361 --> 24:58.230
What?! You f... You fu...

24:58.364 --> 25:00.633
You fucking cu...

25:00.767 --> 25:02.234
Salam Alaikum.

25:02.368 --> 25:03.703
Salazar doesn't know it yet,

25:03.836 --> 25:05.504
but he's going to agree
to a meeting.

25:05.638 --> 25:07.139
It's gonna happen on the island.

25:07.373 --> 25:09.308
That's the only place
he'll feel safe.

25:09.441 --> 25:12.378
It's just a question of when,
but there's still plenty of time

25:12.545 --> 25:14.180
for you and your boys to put
in the infrastructure

25:14.313 --> 25:15.514
and prepare for the worst.

25:15.648 --> 25:16.716
Bronco?

25:17.349 --> 25:18.718
I'm sure you've had
a sniff around.

25:19.118 --> 25:20.152
How do we feel about that?

25:20.319 --> 25:21.554
I think we feel okay.

25:21.954 --> 25:23.022
Okay.

25:23.155 --> 25:24.023
Better get more boots then.

25:30.129 --> 25:31.097
Phase two.

25:31.297 --> 25:32.765
Planning and preparation.

25:39.839 --> 25:41.140
Mr. Beauregard.

25:42.074 --> 25:43.610
Buenos días, Captain Sensible.

25:43.810 --> 25:44.777
Love the shirt.

25:45.044 --> 25:45.812
It's silk.

25:46.713 --> 25:47.513
Like my sheets.

25:48.648 --> 25:49.616
Course it is.

25:49.882 --> 25:51.350
My insurance policy

25:51.483 --> 25:52.118
will need to consist
of a full team.

25:52.251 --> 25:53.886
Baker...

25:54.320 --> 25:55.321
Baker will be in charge
of explosives

25:55.487 --> 25:56.689
and munitions.

25:57.423 --> 26:00.459
Moreno is a wheel man in charge
of on-ground transport.

26:00.827 --> 26:04.096
Dunne is in charge of
aviation... and cynicism.

26:04.330 --> 26:05.564
This is Gucci.

26:05.698 --> 26:06.532
He's in charge of tech.

26:09.736 --> 26:10.937
I just told you.

26:11.070 --> 26:12.772
It's silk.

26:12.905 --> 26:14.173
Their principal agenda

26:14.440 --> 26:15.942
will be getting me
off the island

26:16.075 --> 26:17.343
and should I need
to leave quickly,

26:17.509 --> 26:19.612
they'll need a full chest
of toys.

26:19.746 --> 26:21.848
Indigenous ambulance,
40,000 on the clock,

26:22.014 --> 26:25.384
full tank of laughing gas
and four brand new boots.

26:25.752 --> 26:27.453
Baker, door.

26:29.956 --> 26:31.357
Abracadabra.

26:31.490 --> 26:33.225
Say hello to Javier.

26:33.359 --> 26:35.828
- Hello, Javier.
- Hola, chicos.

26:35.962 --> 26:38.731
He's been a very clever boy
and got the full shopping list.

26:38.931 --> 26:42.935
Two canoes, four oars,
two emergency outboards.

26:43.069 --> 26:47.439
Late 2010 coche,
upgraded with an LS3 V8.

26:47.740 --> 26:50.009
Three KTM 450s.

26:50.142 --> 26:53.379
125 scooter for eggs
and fresh milk.

26:53.579 --> 26:57.917
Two Polaris Razors with 190hp
and plenty of torque.

26:58.985 --> 27:00.319
And Teddy for fishing.

27:00.586 --> 27:02.955
We've got a full set
of knives and forks.

27:03.089 --> 27:04.023
We've got your reach out
and touch me

27:04.156 --> 27:05.424
for the long range slot.

27:05.658 --> 27:08.260
Noise makers, cloudies, blinders.

27:08.394 --> 27:11.764
We've got 9-mils and 45s
avec hush puppies.

27:12.131 --> 27:14.667
Gucci AR with a 203
grenade launcher.

27:14.967 --> 27:17.670
Brand new boom stick
with 40-mil butt plugs.

27:17.804 --> 27:18.905
Top cigars
for the Charlie Gs

27:19.071 --> 27:20.172
for ground to air.

27:20.306 --> 27:21.607
And finally...

27:22.141 --> 27:25.211
24 ice cold
cervezas.

27:25.511 --> 27:26.813
Please drink responsibly.

27:27.513 --> 27:28.647
Alright ladies,
don't get excited

27:28.781 --> 27:29.716
about our accommodation.

27:29.849 --> 27:31.050
It's not the Savoy.

27:31.450 --> 27:32.785
We're hidden in
the most remote part

27:32.952 --> 27:34.353
of Salazar's Island.

27:34.787 --> 27:36.789
We chose this safe house
due to its proximity

27:36.923 --> 27:40.559
to all three extraction points
and its historical tunnels,

27:40.693 --> 27:42.628
should we need to get
Rachel out discreetly.

27:42.762 --> 27:46.098
Rachel is only ever going to be
in one of two places.

27:46.365 --> 27:47.666
Either here at the villa,

27:47.934 --> 27:49.301
or at Salazar's hotel.

27:49.668 --> 27:51.804
He lives in the penthouse suite

27:51.971 --> 27:53.405
which is where they will meet.

27:53.639 --> 27:55.674
If things get exciting,

27:55.808 --> 27:56.743
we extract Mum,

27:56.876 --> 27:58.044
assess the threat level,

27:58.210 --> 27:59.478
bring her back to the villa

27:59.712 --> 28:00.913
and get her off the island.

28:01.047 --> 28:02.715
Three extraction points.

28:03.115 --> 28:04.516
If we need to move
Rachel from the hotel,

28:04.650 --> 28:06.552
we take the east evac route.

28:06.786 --> 28:09.088
We'll take the SUVs through the
town through the storm drains

28:09.221 --> 28:10.689
to two awaiting RIBs.

28:10.957 --> 28:12.759
If we need to extract her
from the villa,

28:12.892 --> 28:14.693
we go from an airfield
on the north of the island.

28:14.827 --> 28:16.162
Jets and helicopters
are a no-go

28:16.295 --> 28:18.330
because Salazar controls
the skies.

28:18.497 --> 28:20.199
That's why we came here
by boat.

28:20.332 --> 28:22.001
We have
two gyrocopters waiting.

28:22.134 --> 28:23.269
They'll go undetected.

28:23.736 --> 28:25.604
The west evac
is our last resort.

28:25.738 --> 28:28.174
There's no other way
off the island.

28:28.307 --> 28:31.110
Each route has its own
challenges but we need to reach

28:31.243 --> 28:33.846
these points as quickly
and efficiently as possible.

28:34.380 --> 28:36.048
We're gonna be ready
for any eventuality

28:36.182 --> 28:37.483
and practice until
we get it right.

28:37.649 --> 28:41.353
But this is Salazar's Island.

28:41.487 --> 28:43.222
The police are on payroll

28:43.555 --> 28:46.658
and he has a reasonably
experienced private army.

28:46.893 --> 28:48.828
- How many?
- Best guess, 50.

28:49.361 --> 28:51.864
- What's that all about?
- Considering his activities,

28:52.064 --> 28:54.433
he takes some comfort
from having a small militia.

28:54.566 --> 28:56.068
The police station
is an issue.

28:56.202 --> 28:57.703
If anyone ends up inside,
we need to know

28:57.837 --> 28:58.704
how to get 'em out.

28:58.838 --> 28:59.872
Where do you wanna start?

29:00.039 --> 29:01.740
Well, first we recce the routes

29:01.874 --> 29:03.609
and then we go look at the hotel
and the police station.

29:03.742 --> 29:04.743
We'll split up.

29:04.877 --> 29:06.012
Gucci, Dunne and Baker,

29:06.178 --> 29:07.780
you recce the north evac point

29:07.914 --> 29:09.548
and log a flight time
to the mainland.

29:09.681 --> 29:13.152
Bronco, Moreno and yours truly.

29:13.719 --> 29:16.155
We'll recce the fastest route
from Salazar's penthouse

29:16.755 --> 29:19.524
through the city
to the east evac point.

29:22.594 --> 29:24.663
Hey, Captain Sensible,
can you, er,

29:24.797 --> 29:26.132
can you just slow down
a little bit?

29:26.265 --> 29:27.233
You're starting
to make me nervous.

29:29.568 --> 29:31.037
Time really does stand still...

29:32.071 --> 29:33.239
when I'm with you.

29:33.372 --> 29:34.406
Dunno what you're
so grumpy about.

29:34.540 --> 29:35.741
You planned the route.

29:38.811 --> 29:41.814
If we're not careful,
your dad's gonna blow our cover.

29:44.383 --> 29:46.952
- Okay. Thank you.
- Okay.

29:46.953 --> 29:48.587
Tell your dad not
to spend it all at once.

29:53.059 --> 29:54.660
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?

29:55.094 --> 29:57.629
That two wheels
is better than four.

29:58.430 --> 29:59.999
Okay, sweethearts,
we'll run the full route

30:00.132 --> 30:01.433
to the east evacuation point.

30:01.567 --> 30:02.434
If we need to get her out,

30:02.568 --> 30:03.669
Mom will be transported

30:03.836 --> 30:05.037
on the back of the bike.

30:11.010 --> 30:12.644
We've got a police car
up ahead.

30:12.778 --> 30:13.779
Who wants to kick 'em
in the ass

30:13.913 --> 30:14.780
and see if they'll kick back?

30:14.914 --> 30:15.814
Leave it with me.

30:15.948 --> 30:16.949
Good man, Moreno.

30:17.083 --> 30:18.217
Try not to end up in jail.

30:26.192 --> 30:27.493
Head to
the storm drains.

30:27.759 --> 30:29.195
See if they have
the stomach to follow.

30:32.664 --> 30:33.699
This is
too fuckin' easy.

30:34.867 --> 30:36.402
What I need is a pig on a bike.

30:44.543 --> 30:46.312
Moreno, what the fuck
are you doing?

30:46.445 --> 30:47.880
You do your thing,
let me do mine.

30:49.681 --> 30:50.917
Looks like your
dream's come true.

30:51.217 --> 30:52.684
You've picked up a pig
on two wheels.

30:52.885 --> 30:54.887
Yep, thank you!

31:01.460 --> 31:04.063
You know, surprisingly he's not
completely shit, this guy.

31:08.034 --> 31:09.401
Let's see if this fucker
likes the idea

31:09.635 --> 31:11.003
of dropping twenty foot
into a storm drain.

31:24.116 --> 31:25.517
Sadly, he didn't follow.

31:25.651 --> 31:26.652
Coming in beside you.

31:32.891 --> 31:34.260
Turns out
you do actually

31:34.393 --> 31:35.627
have some talents, Moreno.

31:43.669 --> 31:45.704
Okay. Looks like
that'll work if we need it to.

31:45.837 --> 31:47.273
So, a boat will
pick us up from here?

31:47.439 --> 31:48.574
That's the idea.

31:48.941 --> 31:50.276
But the bikes won't work
if we need

31:50.409 --> 31:51.877
to take someone
who's incapacitated.

31:52.111 --> 31:54.646
For that, we'll need
the ambulance to get us

31:54.780 --> 31:56.315
through town and an ATV
to get us down the storm drain.

31:56.548 --> 31:58.117
Then we get them off on a RIB.

31:59.085 --> 32:00.786
Okay,
so onto the next route.

32:00.919 --> 32:02.488
North evac is a straight shot

32:02.621 --> 32:04.423
through a wind farm
outside the city.

32:04.556 --> 32:07.559
It is our primary extraction
point as our gyrocopters

32:07.693 --> 32:10.062
are the fastest way
to get Rachel off the island.

32:10.196 --> 32:12.431
We'll need to get these
operational and onto the runway

32:12.564 --> 32:14.200
in no more than three minutes.

32:14.600 --> 32:17.403
The only way to do that
is to rehearse.

32:29.815 --> 32:32.917
It takes 25 minutes
to get to the mainland.

32:32.918 --> 32:34.386
Twenty five minutes?

32:34.753 --> 32:36.355
Give me something faster,
I'll get it there quicker.

32:36.488 --> 32:37.723
How long from the hotel?

32:38.090 --> 32:39.191
Got it down to nine
and a half minutes.

32:39.325 --> 32:40.626
Get it down to eight and a half.

32:40.759 --> 32:42.161
That's not possible.

32:42.394 --> 32:43.862
You're right, six and a half
is possible.

32:43.996 --> 32:45.164
This is how we're
gonna do it.

32:45.297 --> 32:46.198
We'll take Rachel
from the hotel.

32:46.332 --> 32:47.433
These have to be out of the shed

32:47.566 --> 32:49.035
and in the air in three minutes.

32:49.168 --> 32:51.803
You two pilot and take Rachel
and me with you.

32:51.937 --> 32:54.940
If this doesn't work,
we go to the west evac.

32:55.574 --> 32:57.276
That means back to the villa,

32:57.409 --> 32:58.477
through the tunnel,

32:59.178 --> 33:01.613
onto the bikes
until it's easier by foot.

33:01.747 --> 33:03.715
Then there's an obstacle.

33:03.849 --> 33:07.353
The upside of the obstacle
is no-one can follow us.

33:07.519 --> 33:10.322
But the downside of
the obstacle is, er...

33:12.424 --> 33:13.192
That's the straightest line?

33:14.693 --> 33:15.627
Fuck off.

33:16.862 --> 33:18.430
I foresee a problem.

33:18.697 --> 33:20.466
Point A, the villa is two
and a half miles that way.

33:20.599 --> 33:21.800
Point B, the west evac point

33:21.967 --> 33:23.635
is seven and a half miles
that way.

33:23.769 --> 33:24.970
This is the straightest line.

33:27.939 --> 33:30.076
Now, I am aware that
there is a 300-foot deep

33:30.209 --> 33:31.877
untraversable ravine before you.

33:33.212 --> 33:35.147
But fortunately,

33:35.281 --> 33:37.649
Baker and I have put a great
deal of thought into this.

33:37.816 --> 33:41.120
And we've discovered that if you
give yourself enough runway,

33:41.787 --> 33:43.289
build up some speed,

33:43.622 --> 33:45.124
and flap your arms like so...

33:49.961 --> 33:52.131
It should take the bump
out of the landing.

33:54.233 --> 33:57.369
Alternatively, there is another
option for the less adventurous.

34:01.307 --> 34:03.209
It's, er, called a zipline.

34:07.513 --> 34:09.781
The zipline takes us
to where our ATVs are hidden.

34:12.218 --> 34:12.851
Then there's the matter
of getting to the harbour

34:13.018 --> 34:14.686
as quickly as possible.

34:15.087 --> 34:16.855
And like with
the other routes,

34:17.223 --> 34:18.390
we'll need to time
and rehearse this too.

34:21.059 --> 34:21.993
Do it again!

34:37.909 --> 34:39.945
- What happened there?
- I can do better.

34:40.078 --> 34:41.779
Go on. Fuck off.

34:41.780 --> 34:43.615
Jesus! Fuck!

34:44.450 --> 34:45.217
Door.

34:47.353 --> 34:48.254
Four minutes.

34:51.690 --> 34:52.858
Four feet to the left.

34:55.327 --> 34:56.328
Three feet to the left.

34:58.130 --> 34:59.465
Two feet to the left.

35:07.373 --> 35:08.140
Bingo.

35:17.115 --> 35:17.983
Do it again.

35:20.886 --> 35:21.887
Four minutes.

35:22.120 --> 35:23.121
Not too shabby.

35:23.289 --> 35:24.356
Let's go again.

35:27.226 --> 35:28.494
Argh, dammit!

35:32.130 --> 35:33.765
2:59. Got it.

35:33.899 --> 35:35.434
Aaargh!

35:37.836 --> 35:39.905
Three, two, one...

35:45.277 --> 35:46.345
Not bad.

35:53.785 --> 35:55.654
In contingency, if the north
evac fails

35:55.787 --> 35:56.822
and we have pursuing vehicles,

35:56.955 --> 35:59.358
we lead them into a banana pie.

35:59.491 --> 36:01.993
There'll be one vehicle
and two bikes.

36:02.294 --> 36:04.463
Bikes will peel off and ram's
horn behind the pursuers.

36:07.466 --> 36:08.967
You're gonna dig a hole
in the floor.

36:10.001 --> 36:10.902
Question.

36:11.036 --> 36:12.037
What are we digging with?

36:13.104 --> 36:14.139
With your finger.

36:14.840 --> 36:15.907
Or you could use an excavator.

36:18.310 --> 36:20.546
You put the crank arm
twenty yards to the right.

36:20.679 --> 36:22.814
Dusty trap doors
to snag enemy traffic.

36:25.317 --> 36:26.952
- Aargh...
- We drive over.

36:27.386 --> 36:29.054
I'll jump out and trigger.

36:31.357 --> 36:32.691
We'll lose at least one
down the hole

36:32.824 --> 36:34.326
and then whatever's left,
I'll hose off

36:34.493 --> 36:35.994
with the help of the two bikes.

36:36.862 --> 36:38.897
I'll take Mum and continue
to the west evac.

36:39.365 --> 36:40.732
Did the picture
make things clear?

36:43.535 --> 36:44.670
Crystal.

36:47.072 --> 36:48.740
The only time Rachel's
going to be vulnerable

36:48.874 --> 36:50.842
is in transit between the hotel
and the villa.

36:50.976 --> 36:52.844
If she insists on stopping
for ice cream,

36:53.011 --> 36:54.480
we will not be able
to stop her.

36:54.980 --> 36:56.782
So, Gucci, you get the drone up

36:56.915 --> 36:59.251
and everyone else,
invisible but useful.

36:59.651 --> 37:01.086
We do not want them knowing
about the full team

37:01.253 --> 37:02.654
and if they come for a bite,

37:02.854 --> 37:04.890
I want them to lose
their fucking teeth.

37:05.857 --> 37:07.493
We know the evac points.

37:07.659 --> 37:08.960
Speed is our priority.

37:09.094 --> 37:10.362
But because there's
three new routes,

37:10.529 --> 37:12.298
because it is unknown territory,

37:12.431 --> 37:13.932
because it is his island

37:14.065 --> 37:16.001
and because we are outnumbered
ten to one,

37:16.167 --> 37:17.603
we are going to keep rehearsing.

37:17.769 --> 37:18.970
And by rehearse,

37:19.104 --> 37:20.171
he means tick every box.

37:21.440 --> 37:22.308
Tick every tock.

37:23.409 --> 37:24.209
Lube every wheel.

37:25.243 --> 37:26.512
Lick every stamp.

37:27.379 --> 37:31.417
And steal every inch until
all of those routes are ours.

37:31.950 --> 37:34.786
We need to be one step
ahead of Salazar.

37:34.920 --> 37:36.388
We need to know
his movements.

37:36.555 --> 37:38.390
We need to hear
his conversations.

37:38.557 --> 37:40.826
We need ears
in the penthouse suite.

37:40.959 --> 37:42.561
We can only do this
before he knows

37:42.694 --> 37:44.095
that we're on his island.

37:44.463 --> 37:46.398
Dunne will check out
the access routes.

37:46.698 --> 37:49.468
Moreno and Baker will recce
the hotel's rear exits.

37:49.701 --> 37:51.903
Sidney and I will
casually enter the lobby.

37:52.037 --> 37:53.405
Bronco will have
a heart attack

37:53.539 --> 37:55.541
to distract the hotel manager.

37:56.074 --> 37:58.176
She will then kindly
donate her skeleton key.

37:58.777 --> 38:00.479
Bronco will then recover.

38:00.612 --> 38:02.781
- And then Sid will inform her...
- It's low blood sugar.

38:02.914 --> 38:04.350
Just needs a sweetie.

38:04.816 --> 38:05.584
And then my husband and I
will make our way

38:05.751 --> 38:06.852
to the penthouse suite.

38:07.052 --> 38:08.420
Whilst Gucci cuts the cameras.

38:08.554 --> 38:09.488
Cameras are down.

38:17.829 --> 38:18.797
Cameras are off.

38:27.839 --> 38:28.840
Shh.

38:29.408 --> 38:30.241
Hear no evil.

38:34.646 --> 38:35.347
Get it in.

38:37.115 --> 38:38.350
I think I know what I'm doing.

38:51.763 --> 38:52.498
Three exits.

38:53.264 --> 38:54.232
Door we came in,

38:54.366 --> 38:55.467
fire escape...

38:56.301 --> 38:58.203
Or over the edge
for a neck breaker.

38:58.504 --> 39:00.305
If anything relevant
is said there,

39:00.839 --> 39:02.408
or if Salazar loses
his patience,

39:02.541 --> 39:03.642
we should know about it

39:03.875 --> 39:05.811
and we get Rachel
off the island.

39:05.944 --> 39:08.580
If they open fire, we fire back
and we do not miss.

39:08.714 --> 39:11.282
If and when Salazar's police
force turn up,

39:11.517 --> 39:12.350
we make them pay.

39:13.885 --> 39:15.220
How exactly do you
wanna handle that?

39:15.353 --> 39:16.588
Oh, you're gonna handle that.

39:17.456 --> 39:19.290
You're gonna plant engine
killers under their cars.

39:25.196 --> 39:27.699
If anyone ends up
in that station,

39:27.899 --> 39:30.769
we need to know how to get them
out of that station.

39:31.503 --> 39:33.639
And if I recall correctly,
it's your turn to take the tour.

39:37.676 --> 39:38.544
Your boys are here.

39:40.812 --> 39:41.847
They look very athletic.

39:44.249 --> 39:45.517
It's only one night.

39:45.684 --> 39:47.486
Don't overdo it,
as you're prone to.

39:49.888 --> 39:50.922
And remember,

39:51.423 --> 39:52.491
I love you.

39:56.895 --> 39:57.696
Wait for me.

40:00.231 --> 40:01.733
- One more thing...
- Shhh...

40:03.334 --> 40:04.570
Write it in a letter.

40:05.270 --> 40:06.738
But I don't write.

40:06.872 --> 40:08.073
No, not the sombrero.

40:10.442 --> 40:12.077
Oy-oy!

40:12.744 --> 40:13.845
Aah...

40:14.112 --> 40:15.881
La cucaracha...

40:16.948 --> 40:18.617
Sing along with me!

40:18.750 --> 40:20.952
La cucaracha

40:21.186 --> 40:22.821
La cucaracha...

40:22.954 --> 40:25.056
- Are you ready?
- Yeah, we're ready.

40:25.190 --> 40:27.559
- Is it time?
- Yeah, you should get out here.

40:27.959 --> 40:29.928
Did you get me somewhere
nice to stay?

40:30.361 --> 40:31.797
Oh, it's a marble palace.

40:32.363 --> 40:35.166
Frette sheets and gold shitters.

40:35.433 --> 40:37.068
- Liar.
- Whatever you're gonna be

40:37.202 --> 40:38.970
sleeping in is a hell of a lot
more comfortable

40:39.104 --> 40:40.305
than where Sidney's gonna be
sleeping tonight.

40:40.472 --> 40:41.573
Yo! Hey!

40:41.740 --> 40:43.208
Right now, he's er, pissing

40:43.374 --> 40:45.076
on policeman's boots.

40:45.611 --> 40:46.945
Did you get what you need
from Wolfgang?

40:47.445 --> 40:48.947
It's coming.

40:49.581 --> 40:51.950
I just have one more thing
to do. I'll see you soon.

40:52.083 --> 40:54.820
La cucaracha...
Your turn, ladies!

40:54.953 --> 40:57.923
- La cucarach...
- Hey! Hey!

40:58.657 --> 41:00.258
They're ready.
Let's get him to the island.

41:02.227 --> 41:03.729
Let's make this personal.

41:04.362 --> 41:05.263
Let's take his toys.

41:06.565 --> 41:07.866
The jet and the boat.

41:08.166 --> 41:09.701
He'll be flying to the island
on that jet.

41:09.835 --> 41:12.538
Oh, he's a clever boy.
He'll find a way.

41:12.938 --> 41:14.372
Let's go back to court.

41:14.673 --> 41:16.608
The court approves seizure
of personal assets

41:16.742 --> 41:18.744
belonging to Manuel Salazar.

41:18.910 --> 41:20.478
Objection, Your Honor!

41:20.646 --> 41:21.847
Overruled!

41:22.480 --> 41:23.515
First, they'll
ground his plane

41:23.682 --> 41:25.050
under international law.

41:25.183 --> 41:29.287
Horowitz! I'm standing
outside my jet

41:29.420 --> 41:33.024
and being told
it no longer belongs to me!

41:33.158 --> 41:35.627
Y-Yes, of-of course
it's your jet.

41:35.794 --> 41:37.328
It's just a technical issue.

41:37.462 --> 41:40.298
Why can't I fly?
It's my fucking jet!

41:42.167 --> 41:44.636
It's been impounded
under international law.

41:44.770 --> 41:48.774
Since when did I give a fuck
about international law?

41:49.040 --> 41:51.476
And there's a-a little more.
You, you...

41:51.843 --> 41:53.545
I think you might need
to brace yourself.

41:53.812 --> 41:56.214
And then I'll impound
his boat under maritime law.

41:56.347 --> 41:59.651
- He won't even let me on board.
- My boat! My fucking boat!

41:59.785 --> 42:01.119
Now I'll have his attention.

42:01.352 --> 42:03.054
You don't need to worry.
I am confident

42:03.188 --> 42:06.324
that we will get them back...
in court.

42:06.625 --> 42:07.893
We are not
going to court.

42:08.026 --> 42:09.628
I want to look her in the eye.

42:11.830 --> 42:12.964
Set up a meeting on the island.

42:16.635 --> 42:18.069
Vamos.

42:44.362 --> 42:45.664
What took you so long?

42:46.264 --> 42:48.800
I may have overdone it
when I pissed on his boots.

42:48.934 --> 42:49.668
Got any news?

42:52.838 --> 42:55.373
I, er... don't belong
to you anymore.

42:56.374 --> 42:57.475
I don't care about that.

42:59.778 --> 43:00.946
Cameras?

43:01.847 --> 43:03.615
They're connected
but they're unsophisticated.

43:04.850 --> 43:05.951
Guards?

43:06.685 --> 43:08.519
Give or take 12
and about 20 across the road.

43:09.955 --> 43:11.522
- Guns?
- Yeah. Plenty.

43:12.691 --> 43:13.859
Is there any way in the back?

43:14.425 --> 43:16.294
Well, you gotta
blow a hole through the wall.

43:17.562 --> 43:19.698
Next time, you're gonna spend
the night in the cell.

43:20.732 --> 43:23.568
Nah, you're a soldier.
And you're good with the boys.

43:23.702 --> 43:26.037
Yeah, you're right.
They'd eat you alive.

43:26.404 --> 43:28.473
Ooh! On second thought...

43:31.609 --> 43:33.111
I picked up their signal
on the way in.

43:34.479 --> 43:35.380
Abracadabra.

43:36.948 --> 43:39.017
You've got more tricks
than a clown's pocket

43:39.751 --> 43:41.452
and you smell
like a wizard's sleeve.

43:45.891 --> 43:48.694
Here's our police station.
These are our cells.

43:48.827 --> 43:50.295
We can't go in the cell wall

43:50.428 --> 43:52.063
because it's surrounded
by another wall

43:52.898 --> 43:54.432
and it's covered by cameras.

43:54.966 --> 43:57.335
So, we have to go inside if we
want to get somebody outside.

43:57.468 --> 43:58.904
We can go out the back wall.

43:59.304 --> 44:00.605
It's got no cameras and we can
drive straight up to it.

44:00.739 --> 44:01.973
- Ah.
- Drone's found

44:02.107 --> 44:03.274
a nosy visitor, Sir.

44:05.844 --> 44:08.379
Who do we have here?

44:08.847 --> 44:11.016
Oh, ten points if you can guess.

44:11.182 --> 44:12.918
- You gotta give me a clue.
- Big.

44:13.084 --> 44:14.753
- Elephant.
- Bearded.

44:16.654 --> 44:18.389
- Bearded elephant?
- Red.

44:18.757 --> 44:20.058
Red bearded elephant?

44:20.358 --> 44:22.761
Salazar's head of security.

44:27.632 --> 44:28.967
Shall we go say hello?

44:29.868 --> 44:32.037
Nah, I think you're doing
a good enough job.

44:32.670 --> 44:35.040
Phase three.
Conference with an enemy.

44:40.011 --> 44:41.212
Majesty.

44:41.446 --> 44:42.480
Captain Sensible.

44:50.655 --> 44:51.723
Here. This is for you.

44:53.558 --> 44:56.194
Oh... this isn't about
to get awkward, is it?

44:56.327 --> 44:57.195
Just put it on.

45:01.199 --> 45:04.669
Sidney... It's beautiful.
Thank you.

45:04.803 --> 45:05.837
Is there anything in it?

45:06.004 --> 45:07.338
There's a thing in the thing.

45:07.906 --> 45:08.974
If you hold down the button,
no matter where you are

45:09.140 --> 45:10.909
in the world, I'll find you.

45:11.542 --> 45:13.644
I know when mistakes
are made, you need insurance.

45:14.012 --> 45:15.446
Bronco and Sid are mine.

45:21.152 --> 45:23.688
With men like these,
you can't buy loyalty.

45:23.822 --> 45:25.456
It must be earned.

45:25.656 --> 45:27.793
Don't say a word. Follow me.

45:27.926 --> 45:29.727
And I earned that
a hundred jobs ago

45:29.861 --> 45:31.729
when I broke them out
of a prison in Chiang Mai.

45:34.665 --> 45:36.101
- Are we being followed?
- Yep.

45:40.772 --> 45:42.373
- Do we care?
- No.

45:44.509 --> 45:46.544
Is there a reason
why we're driving so slow?

45:46.677 --> 45:49.147
Dangerous things happen
to people who drive too fast.

45:49.280 --> 45:50.748
And I wouldn't want them
to get in an accident.

46:07.833 --> 46:09.134
- Hello.
- Ma'am.

46:12.137 --> 46:14.272
- Mr. Beauregard.
- Sir.

46:16.074 --> 46:20.111
So, marble palace,
Frette sheets, golden shitter?

46:20.311 --> 46:22.080
Oh no, that's for the kids.

46:22.613 --> 46:25.150
For you, ma'am,
we have 100% electric RV,

46:25.283 --> 46:27.352
organic sheets
and a compostable toilet.

46:27.585 --> 46:28.486
Let me give you a tour.

46:29.220 --> 46:29.955
Kids.

46:31.122 --> 46:32.157
Ma'am.

46:56.514 --> 46:58.183
We start at 350.

46:58.349 --> 47:00.218
Nudge it to four if we have to.

47:00.751 --> 47:02.353
I think you should start...

47:04.589 --> 47:06.457
Gucci, any news?

47:06.591 --> 47:09.160
Ma'am, it sounds like
their final number is 400.

47:09.460 --> 47:10.361
That's not gonna cut it.

47:43.962 --> 47:45.530
Señor Salazar. Rachel Wild.

47:48.366 --> 47:49.567
Miss Wild.

47:50.735 --> 47:55.140
My client is prepared
to increase the previous offer.

47:55.573 --> 47:57.242
Well, we're not losing
any time then.

47:59.510 --> 48:04.115
Mr. Salazar is offering
$350 million

48:04.515 --> 48:06.317
to wrap this up today.

48:06.751 --> 48:08.386
Well, I'm prepared
to be here till midnight

48:08.553 --> 48:10.355
to find a way through
this challenge.

48:10.755 --> 48:14.993
But, in the spirit of brevity,
throw a sharper dart.

48:16.061 --> 48:16.827
Four hundred.

48:18.429 --> 48:20.031
You won't get any more
than that.

48:20.165 --> 48:21.366
Mr. Salazar, we agreed
to stick to the...

48:21.499 --> 48:23.868
- Shut up, Horowitz.
- Oh.

48:24.002 --> 48:26.236
Well, the games begin.

48:26.237 --> 48:28.739
We move from the tail
to the dog.

48:34.779 --> 48:38.116
You crossed the line,
Miss Wild. You play dirty.

48:39.084 --> 48:42.787
For the first time in 15 years
I travelled to this meeting

48:42.920 --> 48:44.555
in a jet that
didn't belong to me.

48:47.858 --> 48:52.197
Why? Because someone didn't
respect the rules of the game.

48:53.764 --> 48:55.633
Someone thought
they were clever.

48:56.034 --> 48:58.569
But there is a line
separating business wealth

48:58.703 --> 49:00.271
and personal assets.

49:01.039 --> 49:03.074
Spencer Goldstein invested
in my business,

49:04.042 --> 49:05.476
not in my personal space.

49:07.112 --> 49:10.647
But you have marched an army
across that line.

49:10.648 --> 49:12.650
Oh... wait.

49:15.720 --> 49:16.954
I have an image.

49:18.056 --> 49:20.258
Of a maiden in distress
clutching her pearls.

49:20.391 --> 49:21.959
I too have an image.

49:22.727 --> 49:25.596
But I would not be a gentleman
if I shared it with you.

49:25.896 --> 49:26.964
The debt is a billion dollars.

49:27.098 --> 49:28.233
I'm just here to help you

49:28.399 --> 49:29.800
facilitate in any way I can

49:29.934 --> 49:32.070
you satisfying that obligation.

49:32.270 --> 49:34.972
I am conscious of the small
print and I don't want you

49:35.106 --> 49:37.842
to incur surcharges,
penalties, interest.

49:39.810 --> 49:42.113
I'm also known to be
a rather effective nuisance.

49:43.914 --> 49:45.350
Your blade has reached its hilt.

49:46.351 --> 49:47.652
You can't cut any deeper.

49:49.520 --> 49:51.289
Take what's on the table
and fuck off.

50:08.839 --> 50:10.975
Fuck... I need a drink.

50:19.317 --> 50:20.985
- Glover?
- Boss.

50:21.219 --> 50:23.821
I need more information.
I can't get him to budge.

50:23.954 --> 50:26.057
We don't have the leverage
and he knows it.

50:26.191 --> 50:29.360
Look, unless
Wolfgang opens up more files,

50:29.494 --> 50:30.461
we've bottomed out.

50:33.198 --> 50:34.132
I want a beer.

50:35.633 --> 50:36.467
Understood.

50:37.635 --> 50:39.304
We're making a quick pitstop.

50:39.470 --> 50:41.272
- What are we doing?
- Boss wants a beer.

50:41.406 --> 50:43.174
Hell of a time
for a fuckin' beer.

50:43.574 --> 50:45.710
- Arrivederci, mon amour.
- Don't have too much fun.

50:49.680 --> 50:51.516
Mum and Bronco are heading
into the café.

50:51.649 --> 50:54.018
Let's secure the perimeter.
Gucci, get the drone up.

50:54.752 --> 50:55.720
Just pulled up.

50:58.323 --> 50:59.824
Are we all invited
for a beer?

51:00.191 --> 51:02.193
- Dunne, what's your ETA?
- I'm a minute out.

51:02.327 --> 51:04.229
Reserved a table
in the back for us.

51:04.495 --> 51:05.696
How romantic.

51:06.531 --> 51:07.798
Dunne, on your arrival,

51:08.166 --> 51:09.134
cover the east side
of the square.

51:09.267 --> 51:10.735
- Copy.
- Hm...

51:12.503 --> 51:14.372
Gucci, how we looking?

51:14.739 --> 51:15.540
Checking now.

51:18.243 --> 51:20.211
A lot of movement
coming towards the café.

51:20.711 --> 51:23.214
- Buenas. ¿Qué les ponemos?
- Dos cervezas, por favor.

51:23.348 --> 51:24.615
Perfecto.

51:25.750 --> 51:28.686
- How are we doing, Sid?
- Starting to smell a bit fishy.

51:31.356 --> 51:33.158
See those two muppets
entering the café now?

51:33.524 --> 51:34.859
They were at Salazar's hotel.

51:35.926 --> 51:37.562
Bronco, two of Salazar's
guests joining you.

51:38.896 --> 51:39.564
Do you have them?

51:41.732 --> 51:43.100
Yeah, got eyes on 'em.

51:46.036 --> 51:48.173
Well, this might be more complex
than I thought.

51:48.306 --> 51:49.840
Well, you like complex.

51:50.241 --> 51:51.108
Sid, there's two more
entering the bar.

51:51.242 --> 51:52.410
Okay.

51:53.378 --> 51:55.613
Bronco, two new customers.
Side door. Bar area.

51:55.746 --> 51:56.714
Do you have eyes on?

51:57.915 --> 51:58.649
Eyes on.

52:00.585 --> 52:02.387
Two more hostiles
outside the bar.

52:02.587 --> 52:05.089
Bronco, it's getting congested.

52:05.390 --> 52:07.258
- Baker, you take the bar.
- Baker, you're on.

52:07.425 --> 52:08.493
I'm bringing the car
to the rear of the café.

52:08.659 --> 52:09.760
Right.

52:09.894 --> 52:10.661
Bronco, you're taking her

52:10.828 --> 52:11.629
out the back door.

52:12.830 --> 52:14.399
Approaching bar entrance.

52:14.765 --> 52:16.701
- Thank you.
- Just gonna borrow this.

52:21.239 --> 52:23.107
Bronco,
how are we looking in there?

52:23.841 --> 52:26.143
Yeah, we got two in the lobby,
we've got one in the back bar

52:26.277 --> 52:27.512
and one in the corridor.

52:28.246 --> 52:30.414
Do we have a problem?

52:30.415 --> 52:32.850
Hm... more of a challenge
than a problem.

52:34.352 --> 52:36.887
Hush puppies on,
we keep this quiet.

52:37.021 --> 52:38.155
Copy.

52:39.123 --> 52:41.392
Mexico, you've got two bogies
coming from behind you.

52:41.526 --> 52:42.760
I'm on 'em.

52:43.027 --> 52:45.129
- Eyes on, Guch?
- Two more incoming.

52:45.263 --> 52:46.897
It's an entire fucking
football team.

52:47.031 --> 52:48.999
Dunne, stand by.

52:49.133 --> 52:50.501
Anyone else's pants
getting tighter?

52:50.635 --> 52:51.602
Gucci, sit rep?

52:51.769 --> 52:52.803
Four sitting out front.

52:52.937 --> 52:53.938
Four inside.

52:54.972 --> 52:56.907
Sidney, the back door's
still clear.

52:57.708 --> 53:00.010
I'll leave the car running
at the back door.

53:00.144 --> 53:01.546
Entering the rear
of the building.

53:01.679 --> 53:03.581
Got an Escalade inbound.

53:04.382 --> 53:06.150
There's at least
six on board.

53:06.284 --> 53:07.985
By my count,
that's 14 unfriendlies.

53:08.118 --> 53:08.919
You set out there?

53:09.053 --> 53:10.187
Yep, ready when you are.

53:12.623 --> 53:14.259
They'll be going
for an extraction.

53:14.392 --> 53:17.194
Moving to the kitchen entrance.
On your command, Bronco.

53:17.962 --> 53:22.031
Alright. I'm gonna take
the two in the lobby.

53:22.032 --> 53:23.634
Sid, you take
the back bar.

53:24.302 --> 53:26.036
Baker, take the corridor.

53:28.306 --> 53:29.374
Weapons are free.

53:48.593 --> 53:51.462
Two down. Lobby clear.

53:51.596 --> 53:53.364
- Kitchen clear.
- Bar clear.

53:54.231 --> 53:56.233
Let's go.

53:56.367 --> 53:57.668
Gucci, are we good?

53:57.868 --> 53:59.537
Bronco, back door's clear. Go.

54:00.271 --> 54:01.272
They're exiting
the Escalade.

54:02.707 --> 54:04.275
Go out the rear.

54:06.377 --> 54:07.545
Engaging front entrance.

54:09.747 --> 54:10.981
They're down!

54:11.115 --> 54:13.117
Escalade, clear. Baker?

54:15.353 --> 54:16.053
Clear.

54:18.289 --> 54:19.457
Extracting Mom now.

54:22.192 --> 54:23.628
Good shooting.
Let's pack this up.

54:29.300 --> 54:31.235
Bronco, you've got two
on a scooter.

54:37.074 --> 54:38.275
- Bronco's clear.
- Let's go.

54:40.545 --> 54:41.646
Get in. Lay down.

54:43.648 --> 54:45.550
Gucci, let's get
out of here.

54:45.716 --> 54:46.584
Pulling up.

54:49.987 --> 54:51.589
Bronco, we good?

54:51.989 --> 54:54.158
We're good. Mom's secure.
Rendezvous at the villa.

54:56.260 --> 54:57.828
Gucci, back to the villa.

54:58.062 --> 55:00.164
No wheelspins, no speeding,
don't run any red lights.

55:00.297 --> 55:02.367
Dunne, if anyone tries to stop
you, shoot them in the face.

55:14.311 --> 55:15.413
It didn't work.

55:17.181 --> 55:19.083
W-what didn't work?

55:19.984 --> 55:20.951
Fourteen men.

55:22.286 --> 55:24.655
- Fourteen men?
- Fourteen.

55:24.789 --> 55:25.990
What do you mean,
"fourteen men"?

55:29.159 --> 55:31.161
Don't tell me you've fallen
into her trap.

55:34.532 --> 55:36.200
If you tried
to kill her,

55:36.333 --> 55:38.135
she'll get
an emergency injunction.

55:39.970 --> 55:41.972
That will turn us upside down.

55:44.609 --> 55:47.311
Legally, they'll be able
to see everything.

55:49.013 --> 55:50.848
Get Wolfgang on the phone, now.

56:05.229 --> 56:06.263
Boss?

56:06.631 --> 56:08.433
Glover, talk to me.

56:08.799 --> 56:11.702
Wolfgang's moving assets.
Big assets.

56:12.236 --> 56:13.003
They're panicking.

56:16.206 --> 56:18.142
I think we've got him.

56:18.308 --> 56:20.745
Glover, I fucking love you.

56:21.145 --> 56:23.481
Listen to me, this is what
you're gonna do.

56:24.649 --> 56:27.017
Connect the assets
to his hidden businesses.

56:27.151 --> 56:29.420
Attach them to his name
and shut them down.

56:29.654 --> 56:31.889
We can crack the code
and read the cipher.

56:32.256 --> 56:34.592
If we cut off his income
streams, he'll have no choice

56:34.725 --> 56:37.294
but to come back to the table
and pay the full billion.

56:37.528 --> 56:39.430
If you're all in, we're all in.

56:40.965 --> 56:43.033
But if you want out,
we can get you out.

56:43.834 --> 56:44.569
Right now.

56:46.103 --> 56:47.304
We're staying.

56:47.672 --> 56:49.740
Sidney, the gift
you gave Wolfgang

56:49.874 --> 56:51.542
is the gift that kept on giving.

56:51.676 --> 56:54.378
What started with a drip
ended in a deluge.

56:54.612 --> 56:58.148
Now I know what Salazar's got
and where he's hiding it.

56:58.516 --> 57:02.620
And my lawyers are gonna freeze,
seize and bleed him dry.

57:02.753 --> 57:04.989
The court approves
the application to seek

57:05.122 --> 57:06.223
international
attachment orders.

57:07.391 --> 57:08.993
He'll be fucked.

57:09.126 --> 57:12.162
Next, Skyecill,
chemical manufacturing.

57:12.296 --> 57:14.398
Turnover $1.1 billion.

57:14.532 --> 57:17.301
Look at the evidence,
Mr. Horowitz. It's unambiguous.

57:17.434 --> 57:19.269
The court approves
the application to seek

57:19.403 --> 57:21.005
international
attachment orders.

57:27.377 --> 57:28.946
The panic will set in.

57:29.313 --> 57:32.016
Primostar Telecom.
His first company.

57:32.382 --> 57:35.820
$800 million in assets.
His walls will close in.

57:35.953 --> 57:38.122
A worldwide freezing order
will be put in place

57:38.255 --> 57:39.289
with immediate effect.

57:39.423 --> 57:40.591
Objection, Your Honor.

57:40.725 --> 57:42.459
Denied. Motion is granted.

57:43.327 --> 57:45.029
By now, they'll know
there's a leak.

57:45.295 --> 57:46.731
I repeat, the motion to lift

57:46.897 --> 57:48.699
the corporate veil is granted.

57:49.166 --> 57:51.736
And finally,
Arkon, digital start-up.

57:51.902 --> 57:54.304
Cash reserve of $385 million.

57:54.438 --> 57:56.440
Freeze...

57:56.574 --> 57:58.275
fuck...

57:58.408 --> 58:00.310
...and seize.

58:00.444 --> 58:03.113
The motion to lift the corporate
veil is granted.

58:03.247 --> 58:04.381
- Objection!
- Denied.

58:04.515 --> 58:06.050
- Objection, Your Honor!
- Denied!

58:06.984 --> 58:08.553
It was only a question
of time before they found

58:08.686 --> 58:09.720
the Trojan rat.

58:09.854 --> 58:10.955
But by now,

58:11.088 --> 58:12.256
we have everything I need.

58:12.422 --> 58:13.758
You have no idea how much this

58:13.924 --> 58:16.126
is going to cost both of us.

58:33.010 --> 58:35.713
Horowitz. What do you want?

58:36.280 --> 58:37.748
My client would like
to see you.

58:37.882 --> 58:38.649
Now.

58:39.483 --> 58:41.151
What, now, now?

58:41.318 --> 58:44.454
Yes, now, now.
That means... now.

58:45.790 --> 58:46.957
I'll be there when I'm ready.

58:55.566 --> 58:58.102
Back into the lion's den.

58:58.235 --> 59:00.170
Well, thanks to you,
there's less lions.

59:09.413 --> 59:13.050
Miss Wild. I hear there
was a regrettable incident.

59:13.217 --> 59:15.252
Well, regrettable for some.

59:15.385 --> 59:17.554
As I'm sure Horowitz
has explained to you.

59:17.855 --> 59:19.189
Once you try to kill me,

59:19.323 --> 59:20.324
you've crossed a legal Rubicon

59:20.490 --> 59:22.126
you can't come back from.

59:22.259 --> 59:24.394
Now, unless you want me to
choke off the oxygen

59:24.528 --> 59:28.065
to any more of the ancillary
appendages you possess,

59:28.398 --> 59:30.334
you'll pay the full ticket
and you'll pay it today.

59:32.002 --> 59:34.138
You can have 800.

59:34.404 --> 59:35.706
What the fuck?
I don't want eight,

59:35.840 --> 59:37.441
I want the full fucking yard!

59:37.574 --> 59:39.143
And I want my boat
and my jet back.

59:39.276 --> 59:41.145
Ooh, a billionaire
without his toys.

59:41.278 --> 59:44.348
An embarrassing paradox!
Get the fuck over it!

59:51.188 --> 59:54.124
Know when you've won,
Miss Wild. Take the deal.

59:54.258 --> 59:57.995
No! The deal is you pay
a billion dollars.

59:58.128 --> 01:00:00.931
For all your chest banging,
have you recovered

01:00:01.065 --> 01:00:02.432
even a single penny
of the debt?

01:00:03.067 --> 01:00:04.935
No.

01:00:05.069 --> 01:00:07.672
You'll accept the deal,
take the 800

01:00:07.805 --> 01:00:09.339
and return my possessions.

01:00:09.473 --> 01:00:11.575
You know I've seen
behind the curtain.

01:00:11.709 --> 01:00:13.443
You have no more secrets.

01:00:14.244 --> 01:00:16.947
So do you really want me
to resurrect all the bodies

01:00:17.081 --> 01:00:18.182
you've been hiding?

01:00:19.049 --> 01:00:21.251
Because I will let slip
the dogs of administrative war

01:00:21.385 --> 01:00:24.288
and I'll share the exact
location of all those corpses

01:00:24.421 --> 01:00:27.557
with every single investor
you've burned previously.

01:00:29.960 --> 01:00:31.896
And it won't be me coming
for a billion.

01:00:32.062 --> 01:00:33.430
It'll be them coming for five.

01:00:45.642 --> 01:00:46.476
The billion.

01:00:48.145 --> 01:00:49.747
And you give everything back.

01:00:51.348 --> 01:00:52.349
We're done here.

01:01:00.758 --> 01:01:01.658
Pay the bitch.

01:01:04.428 --> 01:01:07.231
Your job was to make sure
nothing like this could happen.

01:01:10.467 --> 01:01:12.136
I'm letting you go, William.

01:01:12.703 --> 01:01:14.271
Olsson will take you
to the airport.

01:01:24.214 --> 01:01:26.050
Rachel. How can I help?

01:01:26.183 --> 01:01:27.117
It's done.

01:01:27.284 --> 01:01:28.552
What exactly?

01:01:28.819 --> 01:01:30.554
Salazar's agreed to pay
the full amount.

01:01:32.156 --> 01:01:33.690
That's exactly
what Braxton said.

01:01:33.824 --> 01:01:35.726
Now, there's only two reasons

01:01:35.860 --> 01:01:37.427
why that little red phone
could ring.

01:01:37.561 --> 01:01:39.196
One, you're being fired.

01:01:39.563 --> 01:01:41.265
Two, you're being congratulated
for the brilliant agent

01:01:41.398 --> 01:01:45.269
you hired to help you recoup
your unrecoupable debt.

01:01:45.402 --> 01:01:48.505
If it does, Rachel,
I will be very impressed.

01:01:48.638 --> 01:01:51.575
No, when it does, you'll return
everything we seized.

01:01:51.708 --> 01:01:53.778
Contractually that includes
the jet and the boat.

01:01:53.911 --> 01:01:58.682
- Am I clear?
- Crystal. Consider it done.

01:01:58.816 --> 01:02:03.320
Now, keep looking even harder
at the phone you're looking at.

01:02:05.055 --> 01:02:07.091
Ring, ring.
Mazel-tov, motherfucker.

01:02:16.500 --> 01:02:18.102
So, as I was saying...

01:02:21.038 --> 01:02:23.107
- Bobby.
- Mr. Goldstein.

01:02:25.042 --> 01:02:26.043
Congratulations.

01:02:36.553 --> 01:02:38.122
Bobby, are we really going
to fall out

01:02:38.255 --> 01:02:40.124
over a hundred million?
Call me back.

01:02:43.227 --> 01:02:45.762
Getting money out of Salazar
was a stimulating game of chess

01:02:45.930 --> 01:02:47.998
compared to dealing
with Spencer Goldstein.

01:02:48.465 --> 01:02:50.034
You always said
they could never be trusted.

01:03:00.444 --> 01:03:01.545
Who's that?

01:03:02.079 --> 01:03:03.713
We're a thousand miles
from anywhere.

01:03:04.915 --> 01:03:06.250
- Are we expecting anyone?
- No.

01:03:06.984 --> 01:03:07.818
Rashid?

01:03:09.719 --> 01:03:10.687
Rashid!

01:03:13.423 --> 01:03:15.292
Wait there. Rashid?

01:03:21.431 --> 01:03:22.266
Rashid...

01:03:38.515 --> 01:03:39.316
Shereen!

01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:44.188
Shereen!

01:03:49.326 --> 01:03:50.094
Shereen!

01:04:17.454 --> 01:04:18.488
Hello, my lovely.

01:05:07.671 --> 01:05:08.738
Who the fuck are you?

01:05:12.409 --> 01:05:13.610
You can't just walk
into my office!

01:05:14.544 --> 01:05:15.712
Oh yes, we can.

01:05:15.845 --> 01:05:17.948
I've got security cameras.

01:05:18.082 --> 01:05:18.915
There are people watching.

01:05:19.849 --> 01:05:20.750
No, there aren't.

01:05:22.786 --> 01:05:23.720
So, who are you?

01:05:26.023 --> 01:05:26.723
What do you want?

01:05:28.525 --> 01:05:29.693
Salazar's taken Rachel.

01:05:31.295 --> 01:05:34.231
Oh... all right.

01:05:35.565 --> 01:05:37.901
You're her boys, I see.
Well, that's kind of sweet.

01:05:40.137 --> 01:05:41.305
It's being handled.

01:05:41.771 --> 01:05:42.806
Everything's being handled.

01:05:44.108 --> 01:05:46.376
How... exactly?

01:05:48.578 --> 01:05:49.779
We're dealing with the Ministry
of Foreign Affairs,

01:05:49.913 --> 01:05:51.115
we're talking to
the State Department,

01:05:51.381 --> 01:05:53.083
we're dealing with
the Spanish police.

01:05:53.250 --> 01:05:55.919
It's a... it's a highly complex
and evolving situation.

01:05:56.053 --> 01:05:57.954
So, you're doing nothing.

01:05:58.088 --> 01:06:01.091
Look, we all just
have to be patient

01:06:01.225 --> 01:06:02.959
and Salazar will
get his toys back.

01:06:03.093 --> 01:06:04.928
Rachel gets released.
She gets paid...

01:06:05.062 --> 01:06:06.263
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

01:06:10.000 --> 01:06:12.302
So, you're telling me that
she got you your money back

01:06:12.436 --> 01:06:13.837
and she still
hasn't been paid?

01:06:14.238 --> 01:06:15.405
That's not very nice.

01:06:15.572 --> 01:06:18.242
Look, you stick to the dancing

01:06:19.176 --> 01:06:20.344
and I'll do the thinking.

01:06:20.577 --> 01:06:21.911
Don't be cute.

01:06:22.779 --> 01:06:24.281
Nothing is as simple
as it seems.

01:06:25.182 --> 01:06:26.183
Yes, it is.

01:06:28.318 --> 01:06:29.119
Pay your debts.

01:06:57.847 --> 01:07:01.818
Miss Wild, we made an agreement.

01:07:02.652 --> 01:07:04.720
I kept my side.

01:07:04.721 --> 01:07:06.656
Spencer Goldstein have not.

01:07:06.790 --> 01:07:08.625
No, it's not that simple.

01:07:09.226 --> 01:07:11.161
They have something
really valuable to me.

01:07:11.561 --> 01:07:13.397
Now I have something
valuable to them.

01:07:15.132 --> 01:07:17.701
No, you... you don't.

01:07:18.402 --> 01:07:20.704
Even if they knew that I'm here,
well, they wouldn't care.

01:07:20.870 --> 01:07:22.272
It won't register.

01:07:22.539 --> 01:07:24.741
I'm worth less to them
than a stray dog.

01:07:25.842 --> 01:07:27.911
Quite brilliantly,
you're worth billions.

01:07:29.045 --> 01:07:30.747
But they manage trillions.

01:07:30.880 --> 01:07:32.882
If they owned New York City,
you'd just be a...

01:07:34.551 --> 01:07:36.019
a hot dog stand.

01:07:36.553 --> 01:07:39.922
Holding me gets you nowhere.

01:07:39.923 --> 01:07:41.525
And they're never going
to pay you.

01:07:42.592 --> 01:07:44.161
They haven't even paid me.

01:07:47.164 --> 01:07:48.165
We'll see.

01:07:52.236 --> 01:07:53.537
You will find a way
to make them.

01:07:55.539 --> 01:07:59.309
Otherwise parts of you
are going to start turning up

01:07:59.443 --> 01:08:01.145
in their New York office.

01:08:01.678 --> 01:08:03.313
This is my island, Rachel.

01:08:03.447 --> 01:08:06.015
My police, my law.

01:08:06.716 --> 01:08:08.084
I have an entire army
to make sure

01:08:08.218 --> 01:08:09.519
no-one's coming to save you.

01:08:26.703 --> 01:08:28.505
The tracker's saying she's
still at the police station?

01:08:28.638 --> 01:08:30.307
She's there.
It's confirmed.

01:08:31.641 --> 01:08:33.109
Are we still set
for Plan A?

01:08:33.477 --> 01:08:35.445
Yes, everything
is still in place.

01:08:35.745 --> 01:08:38.315
I've put the engine killers
back on the police cars.

01:08:38.615 --> 01:08:40.350
I've got the zipline working.

01:08:40.584 --> 01:08:42.586
The spikes are back
in their original place.

01:08:43.119 --> 01:08:45.589
So are the landmines.
Even the trap.

01:08:47.724 --> 01:08:48.992
Have the numbers changed?

01:08:49.259 --> 01:08:50.994
Salazar
has increased security,

01:08:51.161 --> 01:08:53.697
so be prepared to improvise.

01:08:53.830 --> 01:08:56.032
There's an extra unit
at the hotel.

01:08:56.166 --> 01:09:00.537
One mobile patrol and
around 20 men at the station.

01:09:00.670 --> 01:09:04.073
Now they change shift, so
there's a perfect time to go.

01:09:04.808 --> 01:09:06.776
But I warn you,
these guys are professional

01:09:06.910 --> 01:09:07.911
and they're ready for trouble.

01:09:10.380 --> 01:09:12.649
Hey. Do you wanna change first?

01:09:19.489 --> 01:09:21.491
We'll lead in the police car.

01:09:21.691 --> 01:09:24.694
Moreno, Baker, you take
the back roads in the Jeep.

01:09:25.295 --> 01:09:27.531
Gucci and Dunne, you take
the RIB to the airfield.

01:09:27.697 --> 01:09:29.065
Everybody clear
how we're doing this?

01:09:29.199 --> 01:09:30.634
- Yes, Sir.
- Stealth.

01:09:30.767 --> 01:09:33.002
Armory. Rachel.
Exit the way we came in.

01:09:33.136 --> 01:09:34.738
And Moreno, you've got up front.

01:09:34.871 --> 01:09:36.973
- Keep eyes out for any movement.
- Copy.

01:09:37.106 --> 01:09:38.942
We'll rendezvous with Dunne
and Gucci at the airfield.

01:09:39.175 --> 01:09:41.811
Dunne, you'll have Rachel in the
air eight minutes from pick-up.

01:09:41.978 --> 01:09:43.313
- Got it.
- Gucci, you've got Sid.

01:09:43.480 --> 01:09:45.482
Then everybody else with me
providing cover.

01:09:45.615 --> 01:09:47.784
And when they are airborne,
we fall back to the west evac.

01:09:48.017 --> 01:09:48.785
Copy that.

01:09:51.288 --> 01:09:52.722
Approaching the rear
of the police station.

01:09:55.692 --> 01:09:57.160
Dropping off Baker to stand by.

01:10:00.196 --> 01:10:02.799
- Bronco, Sid, what's your ETA?
- Thirty seconds out.

01:10:03.166 --> 01:10:03.867
Copy.

01:10:06.002 --> 01:10:07.237
That's Baker on foot.

01:10:10.206 --> 01:10:11.575
Twenty seconds out.

01:10:12.976 --> 01:10:14.844
Moving into position for
surveillance of the front door.

01:10:18.248 --> 01:10:19.749
Ten seconds out.

01:10:20.016 --> 01:10:22.118
Still quiet out front, boys.

01:10:22.252 --> 01:10:25.821
Couple of tangos idling.
Shouldn't be a problem.

01:10:25.822 --> 01:10:27.757
- We're pulling up.
- Copy. Eyes on.

01:10:54.918 --> 01:10:55.685
Ch-ch!

01:10:58.522 --> 01:10:59.923
Manos arriba!

01:11:05.962 --> 01:11:07.897
All quiet,
no movement out front.

01:11:20.209 --> 01:11:21.110
Oh...

01:11:24.314 --> 01:11:25.449
Manos... arriba.

01:11:27.384 --> 01:11:29.885
Manos arriba. Arriba.

01:11:29.886 --> 01:11:31.788
Don't fuckin' think about it.

01:11:31.921 --> 01:11:33.189
Uh!

01:11:39.496 --> 01:11:41.097
We've got incoming, boys.

01:11:41.230 --> 01:11:42.599
One car approaching
the compound.

01:11:45.935 --> 01:11:46.970
Pulling up now.

01:11:50.840 --> 01:11:52.208
He's sitting in the car.

01:11:52.942 --> 01:11:54.310
I'll let you know
when he exits.

01:12:02.619 --> 01:12:03.820
Still no movement.

01:12:06.623 --> 01:12:08.291
Stand against the wall
and stay there.

01:12:15.298 --> 01:12:17.099
Still good on the front door.

01:12:25.141 --> 01:12:27.110
Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah!

01:12:27.343 --> 01:12:29.012
- Ugh!
- Manos arriba.

01:12:29.846 --> 01:12:31.347
Up! You too.

01:12:33.550 --> 01:12:34.951
Three officers coming
in the side door.

01:12:36.386 --> 01:12:37.220
Ten seconds out.

01:12:41.491 --> 01:12:42.158
Five seconds out.

01:12:53.670 --> 01:12:55.639
You've got two more coming
through the front door.

01:12:55.905 --> 01:12:58.174
- Bronco, more incoming.
- It's on you.

01:12:59.976 --> 01:13:01.144
Manos arriba.

01:13:03.513 --> 01:13:04.814
¡Manos arriba!

01:13:11.921 --> 01:13:12.722
Uh, uh, uh...

01:13:17.260 --> 01:13:18.762
Don't fuckin' do it.

01:13:20.196 --> 01:13:21.531
Fuck it!

01:13:24.668 --> 01:13:26.770
You got incoming, boys.
It's starting to get busy.

01:13:26.903 --> 01:13:28.071
We can't get out the front!

01:13:28.204 --> 01:13:29.973
Baker, stand by for plan B.

01:13:41.718 --> 01:13:42.786
Blow the back door!

01:13:44.721 --> 01:13:46.422
Oh, my God.

01:13:46.556 --> 01:13:48.191
- Come on.
- Okay.

01:13:49.793 --> 01:13:51.160
Move, move, move!

01:13:57.133 --> 01:13:58.301
Moreno, get the fucking
car around!

01:13:58.468 --> 01:13:59.636
Movin'!

01:14:08.878 --> 01:14:09.979
Okay. Let's go.

01:14:11.948 --> 01:14:13.583
Dunne,
we are en route to the airfield.

01:14:13.717 --> 01:14:14.684
Get the gyros ready.

01:14:25.562 --> 01:14:26.462
They got the girl.

01:14:28.131 --> 01:14:29.332
What do you mean,
"They got the girl"?

01:14:29.499 --> 01:14:30.767
They broke her out of prison

01:14:31.067 --> 01:14:32.135
and they're trying
to leave the island.

01:14:32.301 --> 01:14:33.302
Well, stop them!

01:14:38.241 --> 01:14:39.643
And get her back!

01:14:42.679 --> 01:14:44.280
If we wanna strand them,
now's our chance.

01:14:47.551 --> 01:14:49.085
Uh!

01:14:54.023 --> 01:14:55.258
Ah!

01:15:16.946 --> 01:15:18.047
Gucci, we are inbound.

01:15:21.384 --> 01:15:22.385
Stay in the car.

01:15:27.824 --> 01:15:28.992
- Moreno...
- On it!

01:15:29.125 --> 01:15:30.226
SUV incoming!

01:15:36.132 --> 01:15:37.567
Drone! Drone! Drone!

01:15:37.701 --> 01:15:39.335
- Get the fuck outta there!
- Dunne!

01:15:39.468 --> 01:15:41.404
Everyone down!

01:15:47.310 --> 01:15:49.746
Dunne! Dunne!

01:15:51.547 --> 01:15:52.381
Argh!

01:16:02.058 --> 01:16:03.559
Argh!

01:16:26.049 --> 01:16:27.450
Gucci, Moreno, get to the bikes!

01:16:27.617 --> 01:16:29.018
On it. Let's go!

01:16:30.419 --> 01:16:32.155
Change of plan! West evac.

01:16:32.288 --> 01:16:34.123
We can't do that.
There's another team incoming.

01:16:34.257 --> 01:16:36.192
Then we'll lose them
in the banana pie.

01:16:37.961 --> 01:16:40.163
Baker, eyes out.
Keep us covered.

01:16:48.304 --> 01:16:49.973
I've got eyes on.
They're one kilometer out.

01:17:10.393 --> 01:17:12.828
Gucci, Moreno, peel off
and prepare to ram's horn.

01:17:12.829 --> 01:17:14.262
Copy.

01:17:23.639 --> 01:17:25.041
Baker, hold your fire.

01:17:25.308 --> 01:17:26.342
Wait 'til they're deep
in the trap.

01:17:30.613 --> 01:17:32.280
A hundred feet out.

01:17:32.281 --> 01:17:33.282
Ram's horn, now!

01:17:34.283 --> 01:17:35.051
Turning now.

01:17:41.624 --> 01:17:43.292
Argh!

01:17:52.435 --> 01:17:53.770
Baker, hold them back.

01:17:57.807 --> 01:18:00.844
Bronco, stopping in three,
two, one...

01:18:03.112 --> 01:18:03.813
Bronco's out.

01:18:06.549 --> 01:18:07.416
Opening the pit.

01:18:09.886 --> 01:18:11.020
Ah, fuck.

01:18:11.320 --> 01:18:12.521
Pit don't open.

01:18:12.722 --> 01:18:13.957
Bronco, I'm running
out of road here!

01:18:14.123 --> 01:18:15.024
Make it fucking open!

01:18:20.329 --> 01:18:21.998
Aaargh!

01:18:23.132 --> 01:18:24.633
Aaargh!

01:18:44.821 --> 01:18:45.755
Argh!

01:18:51.160 --> 01:18:52.428
Bronco, are you good?

01:18:52.561 --> 01:18:53.963
We're good.
See you at the villa.

01:18:56.665 --> 01:18:59.769
Don't worry. There's 70 of us
and six of them.

01:19:00.904 --> 01:19:01.971
Let's go!

01:19:08.511 --> 01:19:09.745
Gucci, drone.

01:19:09.879 --> 01:19:11.747
- Baker, jack-in-the-box.
- Copy.

01:19:11.881 --> 01:19:14.050
Moreno, you'll be with me.
South side.

01:19:14.183 --> 01:19:15.184
Aye aye, Sir.

01:19:15.418 --> 01:19:16.619
We hold them off, draw them in,

01:19:16.786 --> 01:19:18.187
rig this place
and blow the nest.

01:19:20.756 --> 01:19:22.258
Drone is live.

01:19:30.599 --> 01:19:32.335
Three vehicles on the west side.

01:19:32.468 --> 01:19:33.302
Three hundred yards out.

01:19:35.371 --> 01:19:36.472
Stinger, now.

01:19:43.412 --> 01:19:44.647
Twelve on foot
coming your way, Sid.

01:19:44.780 --> 01:19:45.815
They're heading over the ridge.

01:19:49.152 --> 01:19:50.486
Two vehicles, east road.

01:19:50.619 --> 01:19:51.620
Coming towards you, Bronco.

01:19:52.788 --> 01:19:54.323
Baker.

01:20:02.631 --> 01:20:03.967
First car is down!

01:20:04.400 --> 01:20:05.301
Sid, they're cresting
the ridge.

01:20:05.434 --> 01:20:06.435
- Moreno?
- Ready.

01:20:06.602 --> 01:20:07.904
Engage.

01:20:34.097 --> 01:20:35.331
Truck incoming,
east side!

01:20:35.464 --> 01:20:37.300
Another SUV, south east.

01:20:37.433 --> 01:20:39.235
Tactical with an M60
on their back.

01:20:39.368 --> 01:20:40.136
I'll clear up.

01:20:51.214 --> 01:20:53.116
- Baker, open the hole!
- Yes, Sir!

01:21:05.228 --> 01:21:06.162
Moreno, on your right!

01:21:09.798 --> 01:21:10.666
The hole's clear!

01:21:19.075 --> 01:21:20.776
Gucci, Moreno, go ahead,

01:21:20.910 --> 01:21:22.011
set up the zipline!

01:21:22.178 --> 01:21:23.846
- Move!
- Moving.

01:21:25.148 --> 01:21:26.349
Covering. Sid, move!

01:21:30.353 --> 01:21:31.720
Gucci, let's go!

01:21:32.421 --> 01:21:33.957
Check the route is clear.
Leave our ATV running.

01:21:34.090 --> 01:21:34.958
Yes, Sir.

01:21:35.091 --> 01:21:36.359
Move! Move it!

01:21:36.592 --> 01:21:38.094
Move!

01:21:48.704 --> 01:21:50.606
- How you doing, Baker?
- All good.

01:21:51.074 --> 01:21:53.209
Charges are set. We're ready.

01:21:54.010 --> 01:21:54.910
Evac's clear.

01:22:04.187 --> 01:22:07.056
Bronco. Getting meat sweats.

01:22:07.190 --> 01:22:08.324
Shall we ring the bell?

01:22:09.959 --> 01:22:10.626
Thinking so.

01:22:20.869 --> 01:22:21.937
Sid, zipline's up.

01:22:22.972 --> 01:22:25.008
Bronco, Mum, let's go.

01:22:25.608 --> 01:22:26.875
Get Mom out of here.
I'll catch you up.

01:22:27.977 --> 01:22:29.378
No, it's too hot.

01:22:29.545 --> 01:22:31.647
Don't fuck around. I'll stay.

01:22:31.880 --> 01:22:33.482
The plan was you two with Mom.

01:22:33.682 --> 01:22:35.018
Someone needs to stay
and press the fucking buttons.

01:22:35.151 --> 01:22:36.819
- Baker!
- Don't fuck around!

01:22:42.491 --> 01:22:43.259
Bronco...

01:22:44.227 --> 01:22:45.128
Two minutes, Baker.

01:22:45.394 --> 01:22:46.295
I'll be there.

01:22:46.562 --> 01:22:47.330
Two minutes.

01:22:48.664 --> 01:22:49.465
Time to go.

01:22:56.172 --> 01:22:57.406
Rachel, stay close.

01:23:08.617 --> 01:23:09.485
Sid!

01:23:12.621 --> 01:23:13.356
Argh!

01:23:14.357 --> 01:23:15.091
Stay covered.

01:23:26.102 --> 01:23:28.071
Your ATV's running.
We're heading to the port.

01:23:28.304 --> 01:23:29.572
¡Vamos! ¡Vamos!

01:23:42.818 --> 01:23:44.253
Bronco, we need to move.

01:23:44.387 --> 01:23:46.255
Baker,
what's your status?

01:23:46.522 --> 01:23:48.591
- Baker?
- I'm on my way!

01:23:49.458 --> 01:23:51.394
Baker, that's
two minutes. It's time to go.

01:23:51.627 --> 01:23:52.861
I said I'm on my way.

01:23:56.165 --> 01:23:57.866
Get out the front,
the tunnel's compromised.

01:24:06.842 --> 01:24:07.576
Aargh!

01:24:10.846 --> 01:24:12.248
Damn it, Baker! Come in!
What are you doing?

01:24:12.381 --> 01:24:13.716
I'll meet you
at the extraction point.

01:24:22.925 --> 01:24:24.627
- Baker!
- I'm right behind ya.

01:24:24.760 --> 01:24:26.195
You're not fucking
behind me, Baker!

01:24:26.362 --> 01:24:27.830
Get out of there!
That's an order!

01:24:29.398 --> 01:24:30.366
That's an order!

01:24:31.567 --> 01:24:32.335
Fuck!

01:24:35.604 --> 01:24:37.573
Fuck. Just get Mom
off the island.

01:24:37.706 --> 01:24:39.041
What are you doing?

01:24:39.242 --> 01:24:41.444
Don't you do it!
Don't you fucking do it!

01:24:41.577 --> 01:24:43.011
Baker! Baker!

01:25:06.469 --> 01:25:07.570
Aargh!

01:25:10.739 --> 01:25:11.807
Uh!

01:25:31.560 --> 01:25:33.596
Rachel, with me!
Sid, let's go!

01:25:46.409 --> 01:25:47.610
Moreno, Gucci,

01:25:47.976 --> 01:25:49.345
we're two minutes
from the dock.

01:25:49.478 --> 01:25:51.180
Copy. We're ready to go.

01:26:10.433 --> 01:26:11.800
Ah!

01:26:22.345 --> 01:26:23.812
Ah... urgh!

01:26:23.946 --> 01:26:25.281
Shit!

01:26:44.967 --> 01:26:46.201
Go around again!

01:26:53.041 --> 01:26:53.809
Range?

01:26:54.410 --> 01:26:55.210
Wait.

01:26:58.080 --> 01:26:59.014
I said, "range."

01:26:59.582 --> 01:27:00.816
I said, "wait."

01:27:04.152 --> 01:27:07.523
Three hundred. Er, wait, 275.

01:27:07.756 --> 01:27:09.492
- Make your mind up.
- 250. Ram it, Janet.

01:27:13.396 --> 01:27:14.263
Aaah!

01:27:49.898 --> 01:27:50.866
Come on.

01:27:51.900 --> 01:27:52.635
Baker?

01:27:54.136 --> 01:27:54.937
No.

01:27:57.740 --> 01:27:58.641
Take her to the boat.

01:28:00.576 --> 01:28:01.577
We'll catch you up.

01:28:27.169 --> 01:28:29.104
I thought I'd stop by
on my way out.

01:28:31.840 --> 01:28:33.075
No hard feelings, I hope?

01:28:33.208 --> 01:28:34.943
Ah, I've been paid.

01:28:35.411 --> 01:28:37.045
So, everyone's happy.

01:28:37.279 --> 01:28:40.482
Well, not, not quite, actually.
I've come from upstairs.

01:28:40.483 --> 01:28:41.850
So I see.

01:28:42.585 --> 01:28:46.254
Seems like the whole Salazar
debacle continues to unfurl.

01:28:48.023 --> 01:28:49.257
Why do I care?

01:28:49.958 --> 01:28:52.561
No-one knows where he is.
He disappeared.

01:28:52.861 --> 01:28:53.962
We'll catch you up.

01:29:05.474 --> 01:29:06.475
Hey!

01:29:26.161 --> 01:29:27.162
Mierda...

01:29:49.217 --> 01:29:51.086
You crossed
the line, Bobby.

01:29:51.353 --> 01:29:53.522
You should have taken your out
while you had the chance.

01:29:53.656 --> 01:29:55.524
I solved this problem for you,

01:29:55.658 --> 01:29:57.960
but you got greedy
and made a mess of it.

01:29:58.226 --> 01:30:01.530
So, Sid and Bronco are now going
to solve it their way.

01:30:01.697 --> 01:30:03.698
Someone needs to wear it.

01:30:03.699 --> 01:30:05.233
Someone needs to be buried.

01:30:07.002 --> 01:30:08.437
It's not gonna be me.

01:30:09.071 --> 01:30:11.039
Well, let's just hope
Salazar doesn't turn up,

01:30:11.173 --> 01:30:13.241
because if he does,
he'll turn state evidence

01:30:13.375 --> 01:30:14.710
on Spencer Goldstein

01:30:14.943 --> 01:30:16.679
for funding
a criminal organisation.

01:30:16.845 --> 01:30:18.847
Welcome to Miami, Mr. Salazar.

01:30:24.419 --> 01:30:25.854
Who the fuck is Mr. Salazar?

01:30:26.955 --> 01:30:28.023
I'm Mr. Smith.

01:30:29.925 --> 01:30:32.027
As long as that little
red phone doesn't ring,

01:30:33.128 --> 01:30:34.296
I'm sure you'll be fine.

01:30:36.298 --> 01:30:37.232
Love you, Bobby.
